on/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/pi/README.md:\n  Line 12: `scripts/pi/` keeps the Pi CLI runtime mirrors in sync with their `.opencode/` canonical sources. Each generator supports a `--check` drift report and a default write mode that regenerates the mirror. Neither generator modifies the canonical source files.\n\n  Line 21: | `sync-prompts-pi.cjs` | Generates flat `.pi/prompts/*.md` files from `.opencode/commands/*.md`, walking every command markdown file except `assets/`, `scripts/` and `fixtures/` subfolders. `--check` reports drift without writing. |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/graph/README.md:\n  Line 15: `scripts/graph/` contains the CLI entrypoints that refresh and migrate `graph-metadata.json` and `description.json` files for spec folders. It discovers packet folders, derives current metadata, and reports low-confidence fields or drift that may need review.\n\n  Line 50: node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/graph/backfill-graph-metadata.js --dry-run\n\n  Line 51: node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/graph/backfill-graph-metadata.js --active-only\n\n  Line 52: node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/graph/migrate-generated-json.js --dry-run --verify\n\n  Line 53: node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/graph/migrate-generated-json.js --only <spec-folder>\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/loaders/README.md:\n  Line 14: `scripts/loaders/` is the script-side ingestion layer for context generation. It loads explicit structured JSON input, validates that usable session data exists and returns a consistent object for extractors and renderers.\n\n  Line 41: npm --prefix .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli run build\n\n  Line 42: node -e \"const loaders=require('./.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/c