l-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md`](./manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md) | manual scenarios that validate the catalog |\n451: \n452: ### Related Skills\n453: \n454: | Skill | Relationship |\n455: |---|---|\n456: | [`sk-doc`](../sk-doc/SKILL.md) | owns documentation quality, DQI scoring and HVR compliance |\n457: | [`sk-code`](../sk-code/SKILL.md) | owns application-code standards and stack-aware workflows |\n458: | [`sk-git`](../sk-git/SKILL.md) | owns git workflow orchestration, worktrees and PRs |\n459: | [`system-skill-advisor`](../system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md) | owns prompt-time skill routing, including the advisor hook this skill uses |\n460: | [`system-deep-loop`](../system-deep-loop/SKILL.md) | owns the `/deep:*` loop commands that anchor into spec folders |\n461: \n462: ---\n463: \n464: ## 8. TROUBLESHOOTING\n\n(Showing lines 430-464 of 673. Use offset=465 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"│   ├── embeddings/             # Provider implementations\n│   └── ...                     # Chunker, scoring, parsing, utilities\n├── references/                 # Reference documentation (27 files)\n├── assets/                     # Decision matrices, YAML configs\n├── constitutional/             # Always-surface rules (never decay)\n├── feature-catalog/            # Feature documentation catalog\n└── manual-testing-playbook/    # Manual validation scenarios\n```\n\n### Key Files\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| [`SKILL.md`](./SKILL.md) | AI agent instructions: routing rules, gates, validation procedures, template application |\n| [`ARCHITECTURE.md`](./ARCHITECTURE.md) | API boundary contract between `runtime/cli/` and `runtime/` |\n| [`runtime/README.md`](./runtime/README.md) | engine architecture, the public API surface, build and validation commands |\n| [`runtime/cli/spec/create.sh`](./scripts/spec/create.sh) | create spec folders with level-appropriate template files |\n| [`runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh`](./scripts/spec/validate.sh) | run the validation set from the 46-rule registry on any spec folder |\n| `runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js` | update packet continuity state from structured JSON |\n| [`feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md`](./feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md) | complete catalog of implemented features |","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/README.md","text":"│   ├── embeddings/             # Provider implementations\n│   └── ...                     # Chunker, scoring, parsing, utilities\n├── references/                 # Reference documentation (27 files)\n├── assets/                     # Decision matrices, YAML configs\n├── constitutional/             # Always-surface rules (never decay)\n├── feature-catalog/            # Feature documentation catalog\n└── manual-testing-playbook/    # Manual validation scenarios\n```\n\n### Key Files\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| [`SKILL.md`](./SKILL.md) | AI agent instructions: routing rules, gates, validation procedures, template application |\n| [`ARCHITECTURE.md`](./ARCHITECTURE.md) | API boundary contract between `runtime/cli/` and `runtime/` |\n| [`runtime/README.md`](./runtime/README.md) | engine architecture, the public API surface, build and validation commands |\n| [`runtime/cli/spec/create.sh`](./scripts/spec/create.sh) | create spec folders with level-appropriate template files |\n| [`runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh`](./scripts/spec/validate.sh) | run the validation set from the 46-rule registry on any spec folder |\n| `runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js` | update packet continuity state from structured JSON |\n| [`feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md`](./feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md) | complete catalog of implemented features |\n| [`manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md`](./manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md) | manual scenarios that validate the catalog |\n\n### Related Skills\n\n| Skill | Relationship |\n|---|---|\n| [`sk-doc`](../sk-doc/SKILL.md) | owns documentation quality, DQI scoring and HVR compliance |\n| [`sk-code`](../sk-code/SKILL.md) | owns application-code standards and stack-aware workflows |\n| [`sk-git`](../sk-git/SKILL.md) | owns git workflow orchestration, worktrees and PRs |\n| [`system-skill-advisor`](../system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md) | owns prompt-time skill routing, including the advisor hook this skill uses |\n| [`system-deep-loop`](../system-deep-loop/SKILL.md) | owns the `/deep:*` loop commands that anchor into spec folders |\n\n---\n\n## 8. TROUBLESHOOTING","lineStart":430,"lineEnd":464,"totalLines":673,"truncated":true}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/README.md","time":{"start":1788620013304,"end":1788620013319}},"id":"prt_0720f7ef7001Q2cjypK5XHSey5","sessionID":"ses_f8df59422ffeuY8ct2HDJCCEpY","messageID":"msg_0720efada001Fd47J1OnaYZlxT"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788620013328,"sessionID":"ses_f8df59422ffeuY8ct2HDJCCEpY","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_VVH6K9R22usCJ9vC4TuTkewL","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/README.md","offset":1,"limit":270},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"System-Spec-Kit Scripts\"\n3: description: \"Script package entrypoints, source zones, boundaries and validation commands for system-spec-kit.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"spec kit scripts\"\n6:   - \"validation scripts\"\n7:   - \"memory save script\"\n8:   - \"upgrade level workflow\"\n9: ---\n10: \n11: # System-Spec-Kit Scripts\n12: \n13: ---\n14: \n15: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n16: \n17: `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/` contains the shell and TypeScript tooling for spec lifecycle work, continuity saves, metadata refresh, evaluations, setup checks and script regression coverage.\n18: \n19: Current state:\n20: \n21: - Shell entrypoints live in focused folders such as `spec/`, `rules/`, `setup/` and `ops/`.\n22: - TypeScript source folders compile to `dist/` for runtime use.\n23: - `scripts-registry.json` describes script inventory and package-level entrypoints.\n24: \n25: ---\n26: \n27: ## 2. ARCHITECTURE\n28: \n29: ```text\n30: ╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n31: │                    SYSTEM-SPEC-KIT SCRIPTS                   │\n32: ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n33: \n34: ┌──────────────┐      ┌────────────────┐      ┌────────────────┐\n35: │ Operator     │ ───▶ │ Entry scripts  │ ───▶ │ Spec, memory   │\n36: │ or command   │      │ spec, memory   │      │ or graph files  │\n37: └──────┬───────┘      └───────┬────────┘      └────────────────┘\n38:        │                      │\n39:        │                      ▼\n40:        │              ┌──────────────┐       ┌────────────────┐\n41:        └────────────▶ │ TS source    │ ───▶  │ dist/ runtime  │\n42:                       │ modules      │       │ output         │\n43:                       └──────┬───────┘       └────────────────┘\n44:                              │\n45:                              ▼\n46:                       ┌──────────────┐       ┌────────────────┐\n47:                       │ lib, utils   │ ───▶  │ tests and evals│\n48:                       │ shared code  │       │ verification    │\n49:                       └──────────────┘       └────────────────┘\n50: \n51: Dependency direction: entrypoints ───▶ source modules ───▶ lib and utils\n52: ```\n53: \n54: ---\n55: \n56: ## 3. PACKAGE TOPOLOGY\n57: \n58: ```text\n59: scripts/\n60: +-- spec/                  # Spec lifecycle shell entrypoints\n61: +-- rules/                 # Validation rule scripts\n62: +-- memory/                # Continuity save and ranking CLIs\n63: +-- graph/                 # Graph metadata backfill CLI\n64: +-- config/                # Config barrel boundary for script modules\n65: +-- validation/            # Validation, evidence and comment-hygiene checks\n66: +-- spec-folder/           # Spec folder metadata and detection modules\n67: +-- core/                  # Workflow modules\n68: +-- extractors/            # Semantic extraction modules\n69: +-- loaders/               # Data loading module\n70: +-- renderers/             # Template rendering module\n71: +-- utils/                 # Utility modules\n72: +-- lib/                   # Shared TypeScript and shell helpers\n73: +-- evals/                 # Evaluation scripts and policy checks\n74: +-- setup/                 # Environment checks and setup helpers\n75: +-- ops/                   # Healing and runbook helpers\n76: +-- retrieval/             # Trigger-index generator/lookup, ripgrep lane, parity and grep-convention retrofit\n77: +-- observability/         # Smart-router telemetry recording and measurement\n78: +-- codex/                 # Codex CLI agent/prompt mirror generators and drift checks\n79: +-- pi/                    # Pi CLI agent/prompt mirror generators and drift checks\n80: +-- runtime-mirrors/       # Cross-runtime command/agent/hook mirror policy and synchronizer\n81: +-- kpi/                   # Defect-rate reporting for generated continuity support\n82: +-- metrics/               # Deep-loop behavioral efficiency scoring from opencode event logs\n83: +-- optimizer/             # Offline loop optimizer for deep research/review replay data\n84: +-- resource-map/          # Deep review/research evidence to resource-map.md ledger\n85: +-- sweep/                 # Strict-pass freshness sweep CI gate over every spec folder\n86: +-- references/            # Reference docs (e.g. retrieval conventions, runbooks)\n87: +-- tests/                 # JS, shell, Python and Vitest coverage\n88: +-- test-fixtures/         # Validation fixtures\n89: +-- templates/             # Inline renderer sources\n90: +-- types/                 # Shared TypeScript type definitions\n91: +-- check-links.sh           # Wikilink ([[...]]) validator (compat entrypoint -> rules/check-links.sh)\n92: +-- check-markdown-links.cjs # Markdown-link (](path)) integrity guard over skills/commands/agents\n93: +-- deploy-mcp.sh          # Rebuild every daemon-backed package dist\n94: +-- validate-command-tree-parity.sh # Policy-aware runtime mirror gate; explicit arbitrary trees use byte parity\n95: +-- test-council-matrix.sh # AI Council vitest + sk-doc + strict parent-spec validation in one pass\n96: +-- package.json           # ESM package manifest\n97: +-- scripts-registry.json  # Script inventory\n98: `-- README.md\n99: ```\n100: \n101: Allowed direction:\n102: \n103: - CLI folders may call shared helpers in `lib/` and `utils/`.\n104: - TypeScript source may import package-local modules through ESM paths.\n105: - Tests may exercise fixtures under `test-fixtures/`.\n106: \n107: Disallowed direction:\n108: \n109: - Source files should not import generated `dist/` output.\n110: - Shared helpers should not own spec folder policy that belongs in `spec/` or `rules/`.\n111: - Temporary artifacts should stay under `scratch/` or OS temp paths.\n112: \n113: ---\n114: \n115: ## 4. KEY FILES\n116: \n117: | File or Folder | Role |\n118: |---|---|\n119: | `spec/` | Creates, upgrades, validates, completes and archives spec folders. |\n120: | `rules/` | Holds validation checks used by `spec/validate.sh`. |\n121: | `memory/generate-context.ts` | Builds structured continuity save output and metadata updates. |\n122: | `graph/backfill-graph-metadata.ts` | Refreshes graph metadata across spec folders. |\n123: | `config/` | Exposes the script-side config barrel boundary for non-core modules. |\n124: | `runtime-mirrors/` | Keeps runtime mirror exclusions and native command exceptions aligned with generated mirror trees. |\n125: | `validation/` | Contains active validators used by validation flow, pre-commit checks and write-time comment hygiene. |\n126: | `lib/` | Shares TypeScript helpers and sourced shell utilities. |\n127: | `retrieval/` | Generates and looks up the committed trigger index, runs the ripgrep recipe lane, checks retrieval parity, retrofits the grep convention and sweeps for retired-memory-MCP residue. See `retrieval/README.md`. |\n128: | `observability/` | Records and measures smart-router resource-routing telemetry (live wrapper plus static corpus harness). See `observability/README.md`. |\n129: | `codex/` | Generates `.codex/agents` and `.codex/prompts` from their `.opencode/` canonical sources and checks command-router drift. See `codex/README.md`. |\n130: | `pi/` | Generates `.pi/agents` and `.pi/prompts` from their `.opencode/` canonical sources. See `pi/README.md`. |\n131: | `check-markdown-links.cjs` | Repo-wide markdown-link integrity guard over skills/commands/agents; CI-wired via `.github/workflows/markdown-link-integrity.yml`. Strips fenced + inline code before extraction. Complements the wikilink checker. `--self-test` asserts the inline-code handling. |\n132: | `check-links.sh` | Wikilink (`[[...]]`) validator; delegates to `rules/check-links.sh` (opt-in via `SPECKIT_VALIDATE_LINKS`). |\n133: | `spec/repair-derived.cjs` | Repairs the packet facts that are recomputable from disk — recorded location, declared level, generated-metadata fingerprint — and refuses everything else, reporting it by rule. Reporting is the default; `--apply` writes. Skips archived, scratch and pre-rename snapshot trees. See `spec/README-repair-derived.md` for the derived-versus-authored boundary. |\n134: | `deploy-mcp.sh` | Rebuilds every daemon-backed package `dist/` (the spec-kit runtime engine plus `@spec-kit/shared` via TS project references, and the skill advisor daemon) after a source change, then warns about launcher `.cjs` changes that only a fresh session can load. `dist/` is gitignored, so this is the canonical rebuild step after pulling source changes. |\n135: | `validate-command-tree-parity.sh` | Policy-aware runtime mirror gate wired into `spec/validate.sh` as the `COMMAND_TREE_PARITY` rule. Its default mode delegates to the generated mirror checker so runtime-exclusive commands stay excluded; explicit `--left`/`--right` trees retain byte-parity comparison and `--self-test` coverage. |\n136: | `test-council-matrix.sh` | Runs the AI Council runtime vitest suite, sk-doc validation for the deep-ai-council skill, and strict spec validation for the parent council skill package in one pass. |\n137: | `scripts-registry.json` | Lists package scripts and known entrypoints. |\n138: | `package.json` | Defines ESM runtime settings and build scripts. |\n139: \n140: ---\n141: \n142: ## 5. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n143: \n144: Build flow:\n145: \n146: ```text\n147: ╭──────────────────────────────╮\n148: │ TypeScript source folders    │\n149: ╰──────────────────────────────╯\n150:               │\n151:               ▼\n152: ┌──────────────────────────────┐\n153: │ npm run build                │\n154: └──────────────┬───────────────┘\n155:                ▼\n156: ┌──────────────────────────────┐\n157: │ dist/ runtime output         │\n158: └──────────────┬───────────────┘\n159:                ▼\n160: ┌──────────────────────────────┐\n161: │ Node CLI entrypoints         │\n162: └──────────────────────────────┘\n163: ```\n164: \n165: Validation flow:\n166: \n167: ```text\n168: ╭──────────────────────────────╮\n169: │ Spec folder path             │\n170: ╰──────────────────────────────╯\n171:               │\n172:               ▼\n173: ┌──────────────────────────────┐\n174: │ spec/validate.sh             │\n175: └──────────────┬───────────────┘\n176:                ▼\n177: ┌──────────────────────────────┐\n178: │ rules/check-*.sh             │\n179: └──────────────┬───────────────┘\n180:                ▼\n181: ┌──────────────────────────────┐\n182: │ pass, warning or error       │\n183: └──────────────────────────────┘\n184: ```\n185: \n186: This package owns local automation. Long-lived product behavior belongs in the skill docs, runtime package code or shared package code.\n187: \n188: ---\n189: \n190: ## 6. ENTRYPOINTS\n191: \n192: ```bash\n193: npm --prefix .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli run build\n194: bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/<name> --strict\n195: node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js --json '<inline-json>' specs/<name>\n196: # Or use --stdin, or a session-scoped temp file (e.g. /tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json).\n197: # The legacy shared path /tmp/save-context-data.json is rejected (LEGACY_SHARED_DATA_FILE).\n198: node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/graph/backfill-graph-metadata.js --dry-run\n199: node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/check-markdown-links.cjs   # markdown-link guard (exit 1 on broken)\n200: node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/check-markdown-links.cjs --self-test  # guard inline-code self-test (6 cases)\n201: ```\n202: \n203: Use structured JSON input with `generate-context.js`. Do not pass free-form positional save text.\n204: \n205: ---\n206: \n207: ## 7. GENERATED METADATA PRUNING\n208: \n209: Graph child removal uses a mandatory report-then-apply sequence. Run both steps with the exact same scope controls so the confirmation hash remains bound to the reviewed candidate set.\n210: \n211: ```bash\n212: # Single packet backfill\n213: node dist/graph/backfill-graph-metadata.js <spec-folder> --prune-report\n214: node dist/graph/backfill-graph-metadata.js <spec-folder> --prune --prune-confirm <contentHash>\n215: \n216: # Migration scope; repeat the same --root, --only and --limit values for apply\n217: node dist/graph/migrate-generated-json.js --root <specs-dir> --only <spec-folder> --prune-report\n218: node dist/graph/migrate-generated-json.js --root <specs-dir> --only <spec-folder> --prune --prune-confirm <contentHash>\n219: ```\n220: \n221: `--prune-report` is a dry run for generated metadata and writes only its report artifact under the selected specs root. Review every candidate and its `existsOnDisk` state before using the artifact's `contentHash`. Backfill scope is controlled by a packet target or `--all` with `--root` and `--active-only`; migration scope is controlled by `--root`, repeatable `--only` and `--limit`. Apply refuses a missing, modified or stale report.\n222: \n223: Before apply, preserve the affected `graph-metadata.json` files in version control or an operator backup. If validation finds an unexpected removal, restore those exact files and rerun a normal non-pruning refresh. A later refresh preserves persisted lineage by default; it cannot reconstruct a removed stale relationship whose target is no longer derivable.\n224: \n225: ---\n226: \n227: ## 8. VALIDATION\n228: \n229: Use repository-root commands:\n230: \n231: ```bash\n232: npm --prefix .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli run build\n233: npm --prefix .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli test\n234: bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/<name> --strict\n235: ```\n236: \n237: Run targeted shell or Vitest checks when editing one script zone. Use the parent package build after TypeScript changes.\n238: \n239: ---\n240: \n241: ## 9. RELATED\n242: \n243: - [`spec/README.md`](spec/README.md)\n244: - [`lib/README.md`](lib/README.md)\n245: - [`rules/README.md`](rules/README.md)\n246: - [`memory/README.md`](memory/README.md)\n247: - [`evals/README.md`](evals/README.md)\n248: - [`setup/README.md`](setup/README.md)\n249: - [`ops/README.md`](ops/README.md)\n250: - [`retrieval/README.md`](retrieval/README.md)\n251: - [`observability/README.md`](observability/README.md)\n252: - [`codex/README.md`](codex/README.md)\n253: - [`pi/README.md`](pi/README.md)\n254: - [`runtime-mirrors/README.md`](runtime-mirrors/README.md)\n\n(End of file - total 254 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"System-Spec-Kit Scripts\"\ndescription: \"Script package entrypoints, source zones, boundaries and validation commands for system-spec-kit.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"spec kit scripts\"\n  - \"validation scripts\"\n  - \"memory save script\"\n  - \"upgrade level workflow\"\n---\n\n# System-Spec-Kit Scripts\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/` contains the shell and TypeScript tooling for spec lifecycle work, continuity saves, metadata refresh, evaluations, setup checks and script regression coverage.\n\nCurrent state:\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/README.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"System-Spec-Kit Scripts\"\ndescription: \"Script package entrypoints, source zones, boundaries and validation commands for system-spec-kit.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"spec kit scripts\"\n  - \"validation scripts\"\n  - \"memory save script\"\n  - \"upgrade level workflow\"\n---\n\n# System-Spec-Kit Scripts\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/` contains the shell and TypeScript tooling for spec lifecycle work, continuity saves, metadata refresh, evaluations, setup checks and script regression coverage.\n\nCurrent state:\n\n- Shell entrypoints live in focused folders such as `spec/`, `rules/`, `setup/` and `ops/`.\n- TypeScript source folders compile to `dist/` for runtime use.\n- `scripts-registry.json` describes script inventory and package-level entrypoints.\n\n---\n\n## 2. ARCHITECTURE\n\n```text\n╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│                    SYSTEM-SPEC-KIT SCRIPTS                   │\n╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n\n┌──────────────┐      ┌────────────────┐      ┌────────────────┐\n│ Operator     │ ───▶ │ Entry scripts  │ ───▶ │ Spec, memory   │\n│ or command   │      │ spec, memory   │      │ or graph files  │\n└──────┬───────┘      └───────┬────────┘      └────────────────┘\n       │                      │\n       │                      ▼\n       │              ┌──────────────┐       ┌────────────────┐\n       └────────────▶ │ TS source    │ ───▶  │ dist/ runtime  │\n                      │ modules      │       │ output         │\n                      └──────┬───────┘       └────────────────┘\n                             │\n                             ▼\n                      ┌──────────────┐       ┌────────────────┐\n                      │ lib, utils   │ ───▶  │ tests and evals│\n                      │ shared code  │       │ verification    │\n                      └──────────────┘       └────────────────┘\n\nDependency direction: entrypoints ───▶ source modules ───▶ lib and utils\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. PACKAGE TOPOLOGY\n\n```text\nscripts/\n+-- spec/                  # Spec lifecycle shell entrypoints\n+-- rules/                 # Validation rule scripts\n+-- memory/                # Continuity save and ranking CLIs\n+-- graph/                 # Graph metadata backfill CLI\n+-- config/                # Config barrel boundary for script modules\n+-- validation/            # Validation, evidence and comment-hygiene checks\n+-- spec-folder/           # Spec folder metadata and detection modules\n+-- core/                  # Workflow modules\n+-- extractors/            # Semantic extraction modules\n+-- loaders/               # Data loading module\n+-- renderers/             # Template rendering module\n+-- utils/                 # Utility modules\n+-- lib/                   # Shared TypeScript and shell helpers\n+-- evals/                 # Evaluation scripts and policy checks\n+-- setup/                 # Environment checks and setup helpers\n+-- ops/                   # Healing and runbook helpers\n+-- retrieval/             # Trigger-index generator/lookup, ripgrep lane, parity and grep-convention retrofit\n+-- observability/         # Smart-router telemetry recording and measurement\n+-- codex/                 # Codex CLI agent/prompt mirror generators and drift checks\n+-- pi/                    # Pi CLI agent/prompt mirror generators and drift checks\n+-- runtime-mirrors/       # Cross-runtime command/agent/hook mirror policy and synchronizer\n+-- kpi/                   # Defect-rate reporting for generated continuity support\n+-- metrics/               # Deep-loop behavioral efficiency scoring from opencode event logs\n+-- optimizer/             # Offline loop optimizer for deep research/review replay data\n+-- resource-map/          # Deep review/research evidence to resource-map.md ledger\n+-- sweep/                 # Strict-pass freshness sweep CI gate over every spec folder\n+-- references/            # Reference docs (e.g. retrieval conventions, runbooks)\n+-- tests/                 # JS, shell, Python and Vitest coverage\n+-- test-fixtures/         # Validation fixtures\n+-- templates/             # Inline renderer sources\n+-- types/                 # Shared TypeScript type definitions\n+-- check-links.sh           # Wikilink ([[...]]) validator (compat entrypoint -> rules/check-links.sh)\n+-- check-markdown-links.cjs # Markdown-link (](path)) integrity guard over skills/commands/agents\n+-- deploy-mcp.sh          # Rebuild every daemon-backed package dist\n+-- validate-command-tree-parity.sh # Policy-aware runtime mirror gate; explicit arbitrary trees use byte parity\n+-- test-council-matrix.sh # AI Council vitest + sk-doc + strict parent-spec validation in one pass\n+-- package.json           # ESM package manifest\n+-- scripts-registry.json  # Script inventory\n`-- README.md\n```\n\nAllowed direction:\n\n- CLI folders may call shared helpers in `lib/` and `utils/`.\n- TypeScript source may import package-local modules through ESM paths.\n- Tests may exercise fixtures under `test-fixtures/`.\n\nDisallowed direction:\n\n- Source files should not import generated `dist/` output.\n- Shared helpers should not own spec folder policy that belongs in `spec/` or `rules/`.\n- Temporary artifacts should stay under `scratch/` or OS temp paths.\n\n---\n\n## 4. KEY FILES\n\n| File or Folder | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `spec/` | Creates, upgrades, validates, completes and archives spec folders. |\n| `rules/` | Holds validation checks used by `spec/validate.sh`. |\n| `memory/generate-context.ts` | Builds structured continuity save output and metadata updates. |\n| `graph/backfill-graph-metadata.ts` | Refreshes graph metadata across spec folders. |\n| `config/` | Exposes the script-side config barrel boundary for non-core modules. |\n| `runtime-mirrors/` | Keeps runtime mirror exclusions and native command exceptions aligned with generated mirror trees. |\n| `validation/` | Contains active validators used by validation flow, pre-commit checks and write-time comment hygiene. |\n| `lib/` | Shares TypeScript helpers and sourced shell utilities. |\n| `retrieval/` | Generates and looks up the committed trigger index, runs the ripgrep recipe lane, checks retrieval parity, retrofits the grep convention and sweeps for retired-memory-MCP residue. See `retrieval/README.md`. |\n| `observability/` | Records and measures smart-router resource-routing telemetry (live wrapper plus static corpus harness). See `observability/README.md`. |\n| `codex/` | Generates `.codex/agents` and `.codex/prompts` from their `.opencode/` canonical sources and checks command-router drift. See `codex/README.md`. |\n| `pi/` | Generates `.pi/agents` and `.pi/prompts` from their `.opencode/` canonical sources. See `pi/README.md`. |\n| `check-markdown-links.cjs` | Repo-wide markdown-link integrity guard over skills/commands/agents; CI-wired via `.github/workflows/markdown-link-integrity.yml`. Strips fenced + inline code before extraction. Complements the wikilink checker. `--self-test` asserts the inline-code handling. |\n| `check-links.sh` | Wikilink (`[[...]]`) validator; delegates to `rules/check-links.sh` (opt-in via `SPECKIT_VALIDATE_LINKS`). |\n| `spec/repair-derived.cjs` | Repairs the packet facts that are recomputable from disk — recorded location, declared level, generated-metadata fingerprint — and refuses everything else, reporting it by rule. Reporting is the default; `--apply` writes. Skips archived, scratch and pre-rename snapshot trees. See `spec/README-repair-derived.md` for the derived-versus-authored boundary. |\n| `deploy-mcp.sh` | Rebuilds every daemon-backed package `dist/` (the spec-kit runtime engine plus `@spec-kit/shared` via TS project references, and the skill advisor daemon) after a source change, then warns about launcher `.cjs` changes that only a fresh session can load. `dist/` is gitignored, so this is the canonical rebuild step after pulling source changes. |\n| `validate-command-tree-parity.sh` | Policy-aware runtime mirror gate wired into `spec/validate.sh` as the `COMMAND_TREE_PARITY` rule. Its default mode delegates to the generated mirror checker so runtime-exclusive commands stay excluded; explicit `--left`/`--right` trees retain byte-parity comparison and `--self-test` coverage. |\n| `test-council-matrix.sh` | Runs the AI Council runtime vitest suite, sk-doc validation for the deep-ai-council skill, and strict spec validation for the parent council skill package in one pass. |\n| `scripts-registry.json` | Lists package scripts and known entrypoints. |\n| `package.json` | Defines ESM runtime settings and build scripts. |\n\n---\n\n## 5. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n\nBuild flow:\n\n```text\n╭──────────────────────────────╮\n│ TypeScript source folders    │\n╰──────────────────────────────╯\n              │\n              ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────┐\n│ npm run build                │\n└──────────────┬───────────────┘\n               ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────┐\n│ dist/ runtime output         │\n└──────────────┬───────────────┘\n               ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────┐\n│ Node CLI entrypoints         │\n└──────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\nValidation flow:\n\n```text\n╭──────────────────────────────╮\n│ Spec folder path             │\n╰──────────────────────────────╯\n              │\n              ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────┐\n│ spec/validate.sh             │\n└──────────────┬───────────────┘\n               ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────┐\n│ rules/check-*.sh             │\n└──────────────┬───────────────┘\n               ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────┐\n│ pass, warning or error       │\n└──────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\nThis package owns local automation. Long-lived product behavior belongs in the skill docs, runtime package code or shared package code.\n\n---\n\n## 6. ENTRYPOINTS\n\n```bash\nnpm --prefix .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli run build\nbash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/<name> --strict\nnode .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js --json '<inline-json>' specs/<name>\n# Or use --stdin, or a session-scoped temp file (e.g. /tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json).\n# The legacy shared path /tmp/save-context-data.json is rejected (LEGACY_SHARED_DATA_FILE).\nnode .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/graph/backfill-graph-metadata.js --dry-run\nnode .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/check-markdown-links.cjs   # markdown-link guard (exit 1 on broken)\nnode .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/check-markdown-links.cjs --self-test  # guard inline-code self-test (6 cases)\n```\n\nUse structured JSON input with `generate-context.js`. Do not pass free-form positional save text.\n\n---\n\n## 7. GENERATED METADATA PRUNING\n\nGraph child removal uses a mandatory report-then-apply sequence. Run both steps with the exact same scope controls so the confirmation hash remains bound to the reviewed candidate set.\n\n```bash\n# Single packet backfill\nnode dist/graph/backfill-graph-metadata.js <spec-folder> --prune-report\nnode dist/graph/backfill-graph-metadata.js <spec-folder> --prune --prune-confirm <contentHash>\n\n# Migration scope; repeat the same --root, --only and --limit values for apply\nnode dist/graph/migrate-generated-json.js --root <specs-dir> --only <spec-folder> --prune-report\nnode dist/graph/migrate-generated-json.js --root <specs-dir> --only <spec-folder> --prune --prune-confirm <contentHash>\n```\n\n`--prune-report` is a dry run for generated metadata and writes only its report artifact under the selected specs root. Review every candidate and its `existsOnDisk` state before using the artifact's `contentHash`. Backfill scope is controlled by a packet target or `--all` with `--root` and `--active-only`; migration scope is controlled by `--root`, repeatable `--only` and `--limit`. Apply refuses a missing, modified or stale report.\n\nBefore apply, preserve the affected `graph-metadata.json` files in version control or an operator backup. If validation finds an unexpected removal, restore those exact files and rerun a normal non-pruning refresh. A later refresh preserves persisted lineage by default; it cannot reconstruct a removed stale relationship whose target is no longer derivable.\n\n---\n\n## 8. VALIDATION\n\nUse repository-root commands:\n\n```bash\nnpm --prefix .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli run build\nnpm --prefix .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli test\nbash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/<name> --strict\n```\n\nRun targeted shell or Vitest checks when editing one script zone. Use the parent package build after TypeScript changes.\n\n---\n\n## 9. RELATED\n\n- [`spec/README.md`](spec/README.md)\n- [`lib/README.md`](lib/README.md)\n- [`rules/README.md`](rules/README.md)\n- [`memory/README.md`](memory/README.md)\n- [`evals/README.md`](evals/README.md)\n- [`setup/README.md`](setup/README.md)\n- [`ops/README.md`](ops/README.md)\n- [`retrieval/README.md`](retrieval/README.md)\n- [`observability/README.md`](observability/README.md)\n- [`codex/README.md`](codex/README.md)\n- [`pi/README.md`](pi/README.md)\n- [`runtime-mirrors/README.md`](runtime-mirrors/README.md)","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":254,"totalLines":254,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/README.md","time":{"start":1788620013305,"end":1788620013323}},"id":"prt_0720f7ef8001vjzNdWmW1TAB5V","sessionID":"ses_f8df59422ffeuY8ct2HDJCCEpY","messageID":"msg_0720efada001Fd47J1OnaYZlxT"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788620013328,"sessionID":"ses_f8df59422ffeuY8ct2HDJCCEpY","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_JrvgqxQALbmpZeY3m4X2kZH1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/changelog/README.md","offset":80,"limit":25},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/changelog/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n80: | `root.md` | Root spec folder changelog generation. |\n81: | `phase.md` | Phase child changelog generation. |\n82: | Changelog generator script | Reads canonical packet docs and applies one template. |\n83: \n84: ---\n85: \n86: ## 6. VALIDATION\n87: \n88: Run from the repository root after template edits:\n89: \n90: ```bash\n91: bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/validate.sh <spec-folder> --strict\n92: ```\n93: \n94: Generated changelogs should reference available packet docs and avoid claiming task completion beyond those docs.\n95: \n96: ---\n97: \n98: ## 7. RELATED\n99: \n100: | Document | Role |\n101: |---|---|\n102: | [sk-doc changelog template](../../../sk-doc/sk-create-changelog/assets/changelog-template.md) | Global changelog and release-note template. |\n\n(End of file - total 102 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"| `root.md` | Root spec folder changelog generation. |\n| `phase.md` | Phase child changelog generation. |\n| Changelog generator script | Reads canonical packet docs and applies one template. |\n\n---\n\n## 6. VALIDATION\n\nRun from the repository root after template edits:\n\n```bash\nbash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/validate.sh <spec-folder> --strict\n```\n\nGenerated changelogs should reference available packet docs and avoid claiming task completion beyond those docs.\n\n---\n\n## 7. RELATED\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/changelog/README.md","text":"| `root.md` | Root spec folder changelog generation. |\n| `phase.md` | Phase child changelog generation. |\n| Changelog generator script | Reads canonical packet docs and applies one template. |\n\n---\n\n## 6. VALIDATION\n\nRun from the repository root after template edits:\n\n```bash\nbash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/validate.sh <spec-folder> --strict\n```\n\nGenerated changelogs should reference available packet docs and avoid claiming task completion beyond those docs.\n\n---\n\n## 7. RELATED\n\n| Document | Role |\n|---|---|\n| [sk-doc changelog template](../../../sk-doc/sk-create-changelog/assets/changelog-template.md) | Global changelog and release-note template. |","lineStart":80,"lineEnd":102,"totalLines":102,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/changelog/README.md","time":{"start":1788620013310,"end":1788620013325}},"id":"prt_0720f7efd0019BbzNW53Hxbhz2","sessionID":"ses_f8df59422ffeuY8ct2HDJCCEpY","messageID":"msg_0720efada001Fd47J1OnaYZlxT"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788620013328,"sessionID":"ses_f8df59422ffeuY8ct2HDJCCEpY","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_ORY9oBttvRQieJpr8r0PIUNk","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/kpi/README.md","offset":1,"limit":120},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/kpi/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"KPI Scripts\"\n3: description: \"Quality KPI reporter for generated continuity support artifacts under spec memory folders.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"quality kpi\"\n6:   - \"memory quality rates\"\n7:   - \"placeholder rate\"\n8:   - \"contamination check\"\n9: ---\n10: \n11: <!-- markdownlint-disable MD025 -->\n12: \n13: # KPI Scripts\n14: \n15: ---\n16: \n17: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n18: \n19: `scripts/kpi/` reports defect rates for generated continuity support\n20: artifacts. It scans markdown under spec `memory/` directories and emits JSON\n21: metrics plus a concise stderr summary.\n22: \n23: Boundary:\n24: \n25: - Resume source of truth remains\n26:   `handover.md -> _memory.continuity -> spec docs`.\n27: - Generated memory artifacts are supporting evidence only.\n28: - Defect rates are reported, not enforced; callers decide thresholds.\n29: \n30: ---\n31: \n32: ## 2. PACKAGE TOPOLOGY\n33: \n34: ```text\n35: scripts/kpi/\n36: +-- quality-kpi.sh  # Shell wrapper with inline Node.js scanner\n37: `-- README.md\n38: ```\n39: \n40: Flow:\n41: \n42: ```text\n43: quality-kpi.sh -> <active-spec-folder>/**/memory/*.md -> JSON rates + summary\n44: ```\n45: \n46: Metrics:\n47: \n48: | Metric | Flags |\n49: | --- | --- |\n50: | Placeholder rate | `[TBD]`, `[Not assessed]`, `[N/A]` |\n51: | Fallback rate | Generic fallback phrases in generated content |\n52: | Contamination rate | AI process leakage such as \"Let me analyze\" |\n53: | Empty trigger phrase rate | Frontmatter with no `trigger_phrases` entries |\n54: \n55: ---\n56: \n57: ## 3. ENTRYPOINTS\n58: \n59: Run from the repository root:\n60: \n61: ```bash\n62: bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/kpi/quality-kpi.sh\n63: bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/kpi/quality-kpi.sh \\\n64:   \"system-spec-kit/022-hybrid-rag-fusion\"\n65: ```\n66: \n67: The optional argument is a spec-folder path relative to `specs/`.\n68: \n69: ---\n70: \n71: ## 4. VALIDATION\n72: \n73: Use repository-root commands:\n74: \n75: ```bash\n76: bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/kpi/quality-kpi.sh >/tmp/spec-kit-kpi.json\n77: node -e \"const fs=require('fs'); \\\n78: JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('/tmp/spec-kit-kpi.json','utf8')); \\\n79: console.log('valid json')\"\n80: ```\n81: \n82: Expected behavior: the first command exits `0`, writes JSON to stdout and\n83: prints a `KPI Summary:` line to stderr.\n84: \n85: ---\n86: \n87: ## 5. RELATED\n88: \n89: - [`../README.md`](../README.md)\n90: - [`../memory/README.md`](../memory/README.md)\n91: - [`../evals/README.md`](../evals/README.md)\n92: - [`../tests/README.md`](../tests/README.md)\n\n(End of file - total 92 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"KPI Scripts\"\ndescription: \"Quality KPI reporter for generated continuity support artifacts under spec memory folders.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"quality kpi\"\n  - \"memory quality rates\"\n  - \"placeholder rate\"\n  - \"contamination check\"\n---\n\n<!-- markdownlint-disable MD025 -->\n\n# KPI Scripts\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`scripts/kpi/` reports defect rates for generated continuity support\nartifacts. It scans markdown under spec `memory/` directories and emits JSON","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/kpi/README.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"KPI Scripts\"\ndescription: \"Quality KPI reporter for generated continuity support artifacts under spec memory folders.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"quality kpi\"\n  - \"memory quality rates\"\n  - \"placeholder rate\"\n  - \"contamination check\"\n---\n\n<!-- markdownlint-disable MD025 -->\n\n# KPI Scripts\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`scripts/kpi/` reports defect rates for generated continuity support\nartifacts. It scans markdown under spec `memory/` directories and emits JSON\nmetrics plus a concise stderr summary.\n\nBoundary:\n\n- Resume source of truth remains\n  `handover.md -> _memory.continuity -> spec docs`.\n- Generated memory artifacts are supporting evidence only.\n- Defect rates are reported, not enforced; callers decide thresholds.\n\n---\n\n## 2. PACKAGE TOPOLOGY\n\n```text\nscripts/kpi/\n+-- quality-kpi.sh  # Shell wrapper with inline Node.js scanner\n`-- README.md\n```\n\nFlow:\n\n```text\nquality-kpi.sh -> <active-spec-folder>/**/memory/*.md -> JSON rates + summary\n```\n\nMetrics:\n\n| Metric | Flags |\n| --- | --- |\n| Placeholder rate | `[TBD]`, `[Not assessed]`, `[N/A]` |\n| Fallback rate | Generic fallback phrases in generated content |\n| Contamination rate | AI process leakage such as \"Let me analyze\" |\n| Empty trigger phrase rate | Frontmatter with no `trigger_phrases` entries |\n\n---\n\n## 3. ENTRYPOINTS\n\nRun from the repository root:\n\n```bash\nbash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/kpi/quality-kpi.sh\nbash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/kpi/quality-kpi.sh \\\n  \"system-spec-kit/022-hybrid-rag-fusion\"\n```\n\nThe optional argument is a spec-folder path relative to `specs/`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. VALIDATION\n\nUse repository-root commands:\n\n```bash\nbash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/kpi/quality-kpi.sh >/tmp/spec-kit-kpi.json\nnode -e \"const fs=require('fs'); \\\nJSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('/tmp/spec-kit-kpi.json','utf8')); \\\nconsole.log('valid json')\"\n```\n\nExpected behavior: the first command exits `0`, writes JSON to stdout and\nprints a `KPI Summary:` line to stderr.\n\n---\n\n## 5. RELATED\n\n- [`../README.md`](../README.md)\n- [`../memory/README.md`](../memory/README.md)\n- [`../evals/README.md`](../evals/README.md)\n- [`../tests/README.md`](../tests/README.md)","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":92,"totalLines":92,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/kpi/README.md","time":{"start":1788620013308,"end":1788620013326}},"id":"prt_0720f7efb001qKXHf8waJSW4Ho","sessionID":"ses_f8df59422ffeuY8ct2HDJCCEpY","messageID":"msg_0720efada001Fd47J1OnaYZlxT"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788620013328,"sessionID":"ses_f8df59422ffeuY8ct2HDJCCEpY","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_v1a6tICUWYABwIzFBNKB2Kjd","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec-folder/README.md","offset":1,"limit":160},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec-folder/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Spec Folder Utilities\"\n3: description: \"TypeScript utilities for spec-folder detection, alignment checks, metadata generation and nested changelog output.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"spec folder detection\"\n6:   - \"alignment validation\"\n7:   - \"folder utilities\"\n8: ---\n9: \n10: # Spec Folder Utilities\n11: \n12: > TypeScript utilities that resolve spec folders, score folder alignment and generate packet metadata.\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n17: \n18: `scripts/spec-folder/` contains source modules used by continuity save and spec-maintenance workflows. The utilities detect active spec folders, validate content-to-folder alignment, create required packet directories, generate `description.json`, and build nested changelog data for root specs or phase children.\n19: \n20: Current state:\n21: \n22: - Source of truth is `scripts/spec-folder/*.ts`.\n23: - Compiled runtime output is `runtime/cli/dist/spec-folder/*.js`.\n24: - Explicit CLI targets are authoritative when save workflows pass a spec-folder argument.\n25: \n26: ---\n27: \n28: ## 2. PACKAGE TOPOLOGY\n29: \n30: ```text\n31: scripts/spec-folder/\n32: +-- index.ts                 # Public barrel for spec-folder utilities\n33: +-- folder-detector.ts       # Spec-folder detection logic\n34: +-- alignment-validator.ts   # Topic and folder alignment scoring\n35: +-- directory-setup.ts       # Directory existence and setup helpers\n36: +-- generate-description.ts  # description.json generator\n37: +-- nested-changelog.ts      # Nested changelog data and CLI output\n38: `-- README.md\n39: ```\n40: \n41: Generated output:\n42: \n43: ```text\n44: runtime/cli/dist/spec-folder/\n45: +-- index.js\n46: +-- folder-detector.js\n47: +-- alignment-validator.js\n48: +-- directory-setup.js\n49: +-- generate-description.js\n50: `-- nested-changelog.js\n51: ```\n52: \n53: Allowed direction:\n54: \n55: - Continuity save workflows may import through `scripts/spec-folder/index.ts`.\n56: - CLI wrappers may run compiled output from `runtime/cli/dist/spec-folder/` after build.\n57: - Metadata generation may write `description.json` for a selected packet.\n58: \n59: Disallowed direction:\n60: \n61: - Source modules should not import generated `dist/` files.\n62: - Detection logic should not override an explicit CLI target.\n63: - Spec-folder utilities should not own continuity writing or packet persistence.\n64: \n65: ---\n66: \n67: ## 3. KEY FILES\n68: \n69: | File | Responsibility |\n70: |---|---|\n71: | `index.ts` | Exposes the public utility surface for script consumers. |\n72: | `folder-detector.ts` | Finds candidate spec folders from CLI data, prompts and context signals. |\n73: | `alignment-validator.ts` | Scores how well session topics match a target spec folder. |\n74: | `directory-setup.ts` | Ensures selected packet directories exist before downstream writes. |\n75: | `generate-description.ts` | Builds per-folder `description.json` metadata. |\n76: | `nested-changelog.ts` | Builds nested changelog payloads for root packets and phase children. |\n77: \n78: ---\n79: \n80: ## 4. COMMANDS\n81: \n82: Run from the repository root unless noted.\n83: \n84: ```bash\n85: npm --prefix .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli run build\n86: ```\n87: \n88: Expected result: TypeScript compiles and emits `runtime/cli/dist/spec-folder/` files.\n89: \n90: ```bash\n91: node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/spec-folder/nested-changelog.js <spec-folder>\n92: ```\n93: \n94: Expected result: prints nested changelog data for the supplied packet path when the path exists.\n95: \n96: ```bash\n97: node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js /tmp/save-context-data.json specs/<###-feature-name>/\n98: ```\n99: \n100: Expected result: continuity save workflow uses the explicit spec-folder target and supporting utilities from this folder.\n101: \n102: ---\n103: \n104: ## 5. BOUNDARIES\n105: \n106: | Boundary | Rule |\n107: |---|---|\n108: | CLI authority | Explicit folder arguments remain the selected target even if alignment scoring finds alternatives. |\n109: | Archive filtering | Detection filters archived folders before ranking candidates. |\n110: | Metadata | `generate-description.ts` owns `description.json`. Graph metadata belongs to graph-specific tooling. |\n111: | Persistence | These utilities prepare paths and metadata. Writing continuity stays with `runtime/cli/continuity/generate-context.ts`. |\n112: \n113: ---\n114: \n115: ## 6. VALIDATION\n116: \n117: Run the README validator after editing this file:\n118: \n119: ```bash\n120: python3 .opencode/skills/sk-doc/shared/scripts/validate_document.py .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec-folder/README.md\n121: ```\n122: \n123: Run build and a compiled-module smoke check after changing source files:\n124: \n125: ```bash\n126: npm --prefix .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli run build\n127: node -e \"import('./.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/spec-folder/index.js').then(m => console.log(Object.keys(m).length))\"\n128: ```\n129: \n130: Expected result: build passes and the compiled public barrel exports module members.\n131: \n132: ---\n133: \n134: ## 7. RELATED\n135: \n136: - [`../memory/README.md`](../memory/README.md)\n137: - [`../core/README.md`](../core/README.md)\n138: - [`../spec/README.md`](../spec/README.md)\n139: - [`../../README.md`](../../README.md)\n\n(End of file - total 139 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Spec Folder Utilities\"\ndescription: \"TypeScript utilities for spec-folder detection, alignment checks, metadata generation and nested changelog output.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"spec folder detection\"\n  - \"alignment validation\"\n  - \"folder utilities\"\n---\n\n# Spec Folder Utilities\n\n> TypeScript utilities that resolve spec folders, score folder alignment and generate packet metadata.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`scripts/spec-folder/` contains source modules used by continuity save and spec-maintenance workflows. The utilities detect active spec folders, validate content-to-folder alignment, create required packet directories, generate `description.json`, and build nested changelog data for root specs or phase children.\n\nCurrent state:","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec-folder/README.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Spec Folder Utilities\"\ndescription: \"TypeScript utilities for spec-folder detection, alignment checks, metadata generation and nested changelog output.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"spec folder detection\"\n  - \"alignment validation\"\n  - \"folder utilities\"\n---\n\n# Spec Folder Utilities\n\n> TypeScript utilities that resolve spec folders, score folder alignment and generate packet metadata.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`scripts/spec-folder/` contains source modules used by continuity save and spec-maintenance workflows. The utilities detect active spec folders, validate content-to-folder alignment, create required packet directories, generate `description.json`, and build nested changelog data for root specs or phase children.\n\nCurrent state:\n\n- Source of truth is `scripts/spec-folder/*.ts`.\n- Compiled runtime output is `runtime/cli/dist/spec-folder/*.js`.\n- Explicit CLI targets are authoritative when save workflows pass a spec-folder argument.\n\n---\n\n## 2. PACKAGE TOPOLOGY\n\n```text\nscripts/spec-folder/\n+-- index.ts                 # Public barrel for spec-folder utilities\n+-- folder-detector.ts       # Spec-folder detection logic\n+-- alignment-validator.ts   # Topic and folder alignment scoring\n+-- directory-setup.ts       # Directory existence and setup helpers\n+-- generate-description.ts  # description.json generator\n+-- nested-changelog.ts      # Nested changelog data and CLI output\n`-- README.md\n```\n\nGenerated output:\n\n```text\nruntime/cli/dist/spec-folder/\n+-- index.js\n+-- folder-detector.js\n+-- alignment-validator.js\n+-- directory-setup.js\n+-- generate-description.js\n`-- nested-changelog.js\n```\n\nAllowed direction:\n\n- Continuity save workflows may import through `scripts/spec-folder/index.ts`.\n- CLI wrappers may run compiled output from `runtime/cli/dist/spec-folder/` after build.\n- Metadata generation may write `description.json` for a selected packet.\n\nDisallowed direction:\n\n- Source modules should not import generated `dist/` files.\n- Detection logic should not override an explicit CLI target.\n- Spec-folder utilities should not own continuity writing or packet persistence.\n\n---\n\n## 3. KEY FILES\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `index.ts` | Exposes the public utility surface for script consumers. |\n| `folder-detector.ts` | Finds candidate spec folders from CLI data, prompts and context signals. |\n| `alignment-validator.ts` | Scores how well session topics match a target spec folder. |\n| `directory-setup.ts` | Ensures selected packet directories exist before downstream writes. |\n| `generate-description.ts` | Builds per-folder `description.json` metadata. |\n| `nested-changelog.ts` | Builds nested changelog payloads for root packets and phase children. |\n\n---\n\n## 4. COMMANDS\n\nRun from the repository root unless noted.\n\n```bash\nnpm --prefix .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli run build\n```\n\nExpected result: TypeScript compiles and emits `runtime/cli/dist/spec-folder/` files.\n\n```bash\nnode .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/spec-folder/nested-changelog.js <spec-folder>\n```\n\nExpected result: prints nested changelog data for the supplied packet path when the path exists.\n\n```bash\nnode .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js /tmp/save-context-data.json specs/<###-feature-name>/\n```\n\nExpected result: continuity save workflow uses the explicit spec-folder target and supporting utilities from this folder.\n\n---\n\n## 5. BOUNDARIES\n\n| Boundary | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| CLI authority | Explicit folder arguments remain the selected target even if alignment scoring finds alternatives. |\n| Archive filtering | Detection filters archived folders before ranking candidates. |\n| Metadata | `generate-description.ts` owns `description.json`. Graph metadata belongs to graph-specific tooling. |\n| Persistence | These utilities prepare paths and metadata. Writing continuity stays with `runtime/cli/continuity/generate-context.ts`. |\n\n---\n\n## 6. VALIDATION\n\nRun the README validator after editing this file:\n\n```bash\npython3 .opencode/skills/sk-doc/shared/scripts/validate_document.py .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec-folder/README.md\n```\n\nRun build and a compiled-module smoke check after changing source files:\n\n```bash\nnpm --prefix .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli run build\nnode -e \"import('./.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/spec-folder/index.js').then(m => console.log(Object.keys(m).length))\"\n```\n\nExpected result: build passes and the compiled public barrel exports module members.\n\n---\n\n## 7. RELATED\n\n- [`../memory/README.md`](../memory/README.md)\n- [`../core/README.md`](../core/README.md)\n- [`../spec/README.md`](../spec/README.md)\n- [`../../README.md`](../../README.md)","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":139,"totalLines":139,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec-folder/README.md","time":{"start":1788620013307,"end":1788620013327}},"id":"prt_0720f7efa0015xy3IzO7K6rBUB","sessionID":"ses_f8df59422ffeuY8ct2HDJCCEpY","messageID":"msg_0720efada001Fd47J1OnaYZlxT"}}
