044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v3.0.0.3.md:\n  Line 43: | `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/migrate-deep-research-paths.ts` | Added | Migration utility for the path change |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v3.9.0.0.md:\n  Line 45: | `scripts/rules/check-ac-coverage.sh` | Default-on advisory (non-blocking) |\n\n  Line 46: | `scripts/rules/check-scope-adherence.sh` | New advisory scope-adherence rule |\n\n  Line 47: | `scripts/lib/validator-registry.json` | Registered `SCOPE_ADHERENCE` |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v3.2.1.0.md:\n  Line 95: - `bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/validate.sh .opencode/specs/system-spec-kit/025-nested-changelog-per-spec --strict` - PASS\n\n  Line 96: - `bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/validate.sh .opencode/specs/system-spec-kit/024-compact-code-graph/029-review-remediation --strict` - PASS\n\n  Line 97: - `bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/validate.sh .opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/040-sk-auto-deep-research-review-improvement/001-sk-deep-research-improvements --strict` - PASS\n\n  Line 98: - `bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/validate.sh .opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/040-sk-auto-deep-research-review-improvement/002-sk-deep-review-improvements --strict` - PASS\n\n  Line 106: | `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec-folder/nested-changelog.ts`               | Added the packet-local nested changelog generator with root/phase detection and controlled output naming                 |\n\n  Line 119: | `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/tests/deep-research-contract-parity.vitest.ts` | Added executable contract-parity coverage for deep-research                                                              |\n\n  Line 120: | `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/tests/deep-research-reducer.vitest.ts`         | Added deep-research reducer idempotency coverage                                                                         |\n\n  Line 121: | `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/tests/deep-review-contract-parity.vitest.ts`   | Added executable contract-parity coverage for deep-review                                                                |\n\n  Line 122: | `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/tests/deep-review-reducer-schema.vitest.ts`    | Added deep-review reducer and readiness schema coverage                                                                  |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v3.5.0.0.md:\n  Line 139: **Verify and repair with `/doctor`.** After upgrading, the doctor command is the fastest way to confirm each subsystem is healthy. `/doctor <target>` runs a focused diagnostic for `memory`, `embeddings`, `causal-graph`, `code-graph`, `deep-loop`, `skill-advisor` or `skill-budget`. Most targets are read-only and report drift with a recommended action rather than mutating anything. `/doctor:mcp install|debug` covers the MCP launcher and daemon infrastructure, and `/doctor:update` runs a dependency-ordered cross-subsystem alignment with snapshot, validate and rollback. For a quick read-only install check, `bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/doctor.sh --strict` confirms the memory server's dist and native modules are present.\n\n  Line 141: **Recycle the daemon after a dist change.** Because many sessions now share one memory daemon, a pulled change to the compiled server only takes effect once that daemon recycles. `dist/` is gitignored, so rebuild after every pull. `bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/deploy-mcp.sh` rebuilds every MCP dist, and `--recycle` performs the transparent daemon-child recycle that keeps clients connected. A rebuilt `shared/dist`, where the embedding resolver lives, also needs a recycle to take effect.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v3.0.0.4.md:\n  Line 55: 4. Verify: `SPECKIT_ABLATION=true npx tsx .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/evals/run-ablation.ts` should complete without alignment errors\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v3.2.0.0.md:\n  Line 334: | `scripts/lib/validate-memory-quality.ts` | Folder fallback, topic-check skips, sibling relaxation |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2+/v2.3.0.2.md:\n  Line 57: | `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/lib/structure-aware-chunker.ts` | New structure-aware chunker (not yet wired). |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/validation/README.md:\n  Line 16: `scripts/validation/` contains focused validators used by the Spec Kit validation flow, the pre-commit gate and the write-time comment-hygiene hook. The scripts produce structured pass / warn / fail output that shell wrappers and strict validation gates consume.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:\n  Line 438: See [`tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-detection-and-description.md`](tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-detection-and-description.md) for full implementation and test file listings.\n\n  Line 454: See [`tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-literal-naming-ai-derived-slugs.md`](tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-literal-naming-ai-derived-slugs.md) for full implementation and test file listings.\n\n  Line 470: See [`tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-literal-naming-create-sh-fallback.md`](tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-literal-naming-create-sh-fallback.md