{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788620162832,"sessionID":"ses_f8df59422ffeuY8ct2HDJCCEpY","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_10Pnmyz72gA1HhbUPkjsSRQI","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"system-spec-kit/scripts|\\./scripts/|scripts/README\\.md|scripts/spec/validate\\.sh|scripts/spec-folder|scripts/rules|scripts/lib|scripts/validation|scripts/templates|scripts/kpi|\\../memory/README\\.md","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli","include":"*.md"},"output":"Found 32 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/continuity/README.md:\n  Line 82: runtime/cli/continuity/ → scripts/lib/ and shared packages\n\n  Line 215: - [`../../runtime/scripts/README.md`](../../runtime/scripts/README.md)\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/validation/README.md:\n  Line 16: `scripts/validation/` contains focused validators used by the Spec Kit validation flow, the pre-commit gate and the write-time comment-hygiene hook. The scripts produce structured pass / warn / fail output that shell wrappers and strict validation gates consume.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec-folder/README.md:\n  Line 18: `scripts/spec-folder/` contains source modules used by continuity save and spec-maintenance workflows. The utilities detect active spec folders, validate content-to-folder alignment, create required packet directories, generate `description.json`, and build nested changelog data for root specs or phase children.\n\n  Line 22: - Source of truth is `scripts/spec-folder/*.ts`.\n\n  Line 31: scripts/spec-folder/\n\n  Line 55: - Continuity save workflows may import through `scripts/spec-folder/index.ts`.\n\n  Line 136: - [`../memory/README.md`](../memory/README.md)\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/core/README.md:\n  Line 57: workflow.ts -> focused core helpers -> scripts/lib utilities\n\n  Line 84: workflow.ts -> core helper modules -> scripts/lib utilities\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/kpi/README.md:\n  Line 19: `scripts/kpi/` reports defect rates for generated continuity support\n\n  Line 35: scripts/kpi/\n\n  Line 90: - [`../memory/README.md`](../memory/README.md)\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/sweep/README.md:\n  Line 12: `scripts/sweep/` holds the strict-pass freshness sweep, a CI gate that walks every spec folder under `specs` (and legacy `.opencode/specs`), runs `scripts/spec/validate.sh --strict` on each and classifies the result against a prior baseline. A folder that failed with no baseline record is `first-run`, not a regression. A folder that passed before and fails now is a `regression`. This distinguishes genuinely new breakage from a folder that was already failing.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/lib/README.md:\n  Line 16: `scripts/lib/` contains shared helpers for the script package. TypeScript modules compile to `runtime/cli/dist/lib/`, while shell helpers and standalone CommonJS modules are sourced or required directly, with no build step.\n\n  Line 59: scripts/lib/\n\n  Line 160: │ Import scripts/lib/*.ts      │\n\n  Line 181: │ Source scripts/lib/*.sh      │\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/setup/README.md:\n  Line 24: - Full spec-folder validation delegates to `scripts/spec/validate.sh` when requested.\n\n  Line 42: - Setup scripts may call `scripts/spec/validate.sh` for strict spec-folder validation.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/README.md:\n  Line 16: `scripts/rules/` owns the shell modules used by `scripts/spec/validate.sh`. Each rule reports through the shared `run_check()` interface and sets `RULE_*` variables that the validator reads.\n\n  Line 20: - Rule metadata and dispatch order come from `scripts/lib/validator-registry.json`.\n\n  Line 23: - Shell modules stay small and defer shared logic to `scripts/lib/` when possible.\n\n  Line 31: │                         scripts/rules                            │\n\n  Line 40:        └──────────▶   │ scripts/lib/*    │ ◀─── │ RULE_* variables │\n\n  Line 48: Dependency direction: validate.sh ───▶ registry ───▶ rules ───▶ scripts/lib\n\n  Line 92: | Imports | Source shared shell helpers from `scripts/lib/`. |\n\n  Line 93: | Registry | Add or change public rule metadata in `scripts/lib/validator-registry.json`. |\n\n  Line 94: | Ownership | Keep rule-specific checks in `check-*.sh`. Keep orchestration in `scripts/spec/validate.sh`. |\n\n  Line 131: | `scripts/spec/validate.sh` | Shell command | Runs registered rule checks for a spec folder. |\n\n  Line 133: | `scripts/lib/validator-registry.json` | Registry | Defines rule aliases, severity and dispatch metadata. |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/templates/README.md:\n  Line 14: `scripts/templates/` owns the inline gate renderer used to produce Level-specific markdown from shared templates. It evaluates `<!-- IF ... -->` blocks and emits only the content that applies to the requested Level.\n","metadata":{"matches":32,"truncated":false},"title":"system-spec-kit/scripts|\\./scripts/|scripts/README\\.md|scripts/spec/validate\\.sh|scripts/spec-folder|scripts/rules|scripts/lib|scripts/validation|scripts/templates|scripts/kpi|\\../memory/README\\.md","time":{"start":1788620162673,"end":1788620162828}},"id":"prt_07211c66d001b3Gtf3T7cilTHU","sessionID":"ses_f8df59422ffeuY8ct2HDJCCEpY","messageID":"msg_07210d48c001ED45hf7oDZIy4w"}}
