idate-all.sh: line 9: mapfile: command not found\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/.scan-validate-all.sh: line 18: FOLDERS: unbound variable\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/.scan-validate-all.sh: line 44: FOLDERS[@]: unbound variable","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":3,"totalLines":3,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/.scan-validate-all.txt","time":{"start":1788620322259,"end":1788620322283}},"id":"prt_0721435d000196ESh4cf0eMcUs","sessionID":"ses_f8df59422ffeuY8ct2HDJCCEpY","messageID":"msg_072138c02001ulKYawwyB5vb4A"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788620322325,"sessionID":"ses_f8df59422ffeuY8ct2HDJCCEpY","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_0GxdH0cLQhsSorq2gaf7Z5PK","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/continuity/README.md","offset":1,"limit":250},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/continuity/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Memory Scripts: Context Save and Metadata Maintenance CLIs\"\n3: description: \"TypeScript CLI entrypoints for canonical context saves, memory ranking, markdown parsing, metadata repair, and quality checks.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"memory scripts\"\n6:   - \"generate context\"\n7:   - \"rank memories\"\n8:   - \"memory quality\"\n9:   - \"backfill frontmatter\"\n10: ---\n11: \n12: # Memory Scripts: Context Save and Metadata Maintenance CLIs\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n17: \n18: `runtime/cli/continuity/` contains the source TypeScript and Node CLI entrypoints for Spec Kit context saves, ranking, metadata, and quality tasks. These files compile to `runtime/cli/dist/continuity/` for runtime use.\n19: \n20: Current state:\n21: \n22: - `generate-context.ts` is the canonical context-save CLI for structured JSON, stdin, or JSON file input. It writes into the packet's own documents; there is no index or database behind it.\n23: - Maintenance scripts repair research metadata and frontmatter across generated documents.\n24: - Quality scripts parse markdown structure, rank candidate records, and check rendered continuity output before it is accepted.\n25: - One-shot migration scripts remain in this folder only when they still need a documented invocation path.\n26: \n27: ---\n28: \n29: ## 2. ARCHITECTURE\n30: \n31: ```text\n32: ╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n33: │                         MEMORY SCRIPTS                           │\n34: ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n35: \n36: ┌────────────────┐     ┌────────────────────┐     ┌─────────────────┐\n37: │ CLI callers    │ ──▶ │ generate-context.ts │ ──▶ │ core workflow   │\n38: │ node dist/*    │     │ argument parsing    │     │ save pipeline   │\n39: └───────┬────────┘     └──────────┬─────────┘     └────────┬────────┘\n40:         │                         │                        │\n41:         ▼                         ▼                        ▼\n42: ┌────────────────┐     ┌────────────────────┐     ┌─────────────────┐\n43: │ maintenance    │     │ ast-parser.ts      │     │ validators and  │\n44: │ index CLIs     │     │ markdown sections  │     │ ranked output   │\n45: └───────┬────────┘     └──────────┬─────────┘     └────────┬────────┘\n46:         │                         │                        │\n47:         ▼                         ▼                        ▼\n48: ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n49: │ generated packet metadata and the packet's own documents          │\n50: └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n51: \n52: Dependency direction:\n53: runtime/cli/continuity/*.ts ───▶ scripts/core, extractors, loaders, renderers and lib helpers\n54: compiled CLIs ───▶ runtime/cli/dist/continuity/*.js\n55: runtime hooks and slash commands invoke the compiled CLIs directly\n56: ```\n57: \n58: ---\n59: \n60: ## 3. PACKAGE TOPOLOGY\n61: \n62: ```text\n63: runtime/cli/continuity/\n64: +-- generate-context.ts                  # Canonical context-save CLI\n65: +-- validate-memory-quality.ts           # Rendered memory quality gates\n66: +-- ast-parser.ts                        # Markdown heading, table and code block parser\n67: +-- rank-memories.ts                     # Candidate ranking utility\n68: +-- backfill-frontmatter.ts              # Bulk frontmatter normalization\n69: +-- backfill-research-metadata.ts        # Research metadata backfill helper\n70: +-- migrate-trigger-phrase-residual.ts   # Trigger phrase residual cleanup\n71: +-- fix-memory-h1.mjs                    # H1 format repair helper\n72: `-- README.md\n73: ```\n74: \n75: Allowed dependency direction:\n76: \n77: ```text\n78: runtime/cli/continuity/ → scripts/core/\n79: runtime/cli/continuity/ → scripts/extractors/\n80: runtime/cli/continuity/ → scripts/loaders/\n81: runtime/cli/continuity/ → scripts/renderers/\n82: runtime/cli/continuity/ → scripts/lib/ and shared packages\n83: ```\n84: \n85: Disallowed dependency direction:\n86: \n87: ```text\n88: runtime/cli/continuity/ → runtime hook adapters as runtime dependencies\n89: runtime/cli/continuity/ → prompt text or agent-only session state without structured JSON input\n90: maintenance CLIs → silent mutation without an explicit command mode or target\n91: ```\n92: \n93: ---\n94: \n95: ## 4. DIRECTORY TREE\n96: \n97: ```text\n98: runtime/cli/continuity/\n99: +-- ast-parser.ts\n100: +-- backfill-frontmatter.ts\n101: +-- backfill-research-metadata.ts\n102: +-- fix-memory-h1.mjs\n103: +-- generate-context.ts\n104: +-- migrate-trigger-phrase-residual.ts\n105: +-- rank-memories.ts\n106: +-- validate-memory-quality.ts\n107: `-- README.md\n108: ```\n109: \n110: ---\n111: \n112: ## 5. KEY FILES\n113: \n114: | File | Responsibility |\n115: |---|---|\n116: | `generate-context.ts` | Parses save arguments, rejects unsafe temp paths, validates explicit spec-folder targets, accepts `--stdin`, `--json`, or JSON file input, and runs the canonical memory workflow. |\n117: | `validate-memory-quality.ts` | Checks rendered memory artifacts for structure, semantic sufficiency, duplicate risk, trigger quality, and post-save review output. |\n118: | `ast-parser.ts` | Parses markdown into heading, code block, table, and section-aware structures used by memory extraction and validation. |\n119: | `rank-memories.ts` | Scores and ranks memory candidates from JSON input. |\n120: | `backfill-frontmatter.ts` | Normalizes managed frontmatter keys across targeted markdown roots. |\n121: | `backfill-research-metadata.ts` | Adds or repairs metadata needed by research memory artifacts. |\n122: | `migrate-trigger-phrase-residual.ts` | Cleans residual trigger phrase metadata that no longer matches the current schema. |\n123: | `fix-memory-h1.mjs` | Repairs H1 formatting in older generated memory artifacts. |\n124: \n125: ---\n126: \n127: ## 6. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n128: \n129: | Boundary | Rule |\n130: |---|---|\n131: | Inputs | Prefer structured JSON through `--stdin` or `--json`. JSON file mode is valid when the file path is session-scoped. |\n132: | Outputs | Write generated context artifacts, packet metadata, reports, and cleanup results. |\n133: | Ownership | This folder owns CLI surfaces for context save and maintenance. Validation rules, generated-metadata internals, templates, and spec-folder authoring rules live outside this folder. |\n134: \n135: Canonical save flow:\n136: \n137: ```text\n138: ╭──────────────────────────────────────────╮\n139: │ caller provides structured session JSON  │\n140: ╰──────────────────────────────────────────╯\n141:                    │\n142:                    ▼\n143: ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n144: │ generate-context.ts parses CLI args      │\n145: └──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n146:                    │\n147:                    ▼\n148: ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n149: │ validate explicit spec-folder target     │\n150: └──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n151:                    │\n152:                    ▼\n153: ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n154: │ load collected data and session details  │\n155: └──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n156:                    │\n157:                    ▼\n158: ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n159: │ run core continuity workflow             │\n160: └──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n161:                    │\n162:                    ▼\n163: ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n164: │ validate rendered continuity quality     │\n165: └──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n166:                    │\n167:                    ▼\n168: ╭──────────────────────────────────────────╮\n169: │ the packet's documents and generated     │\n170: │ metadata are updated; the save ends here │\n171: ╰──────────────────────────────────────────╯\n172: ```\n173: \n174: ---\n175: \n176: ## 7. ENTRYPOINTS\n177: \n178: Run compiled commands from the repository root after the TypeScript build has produced `runtime/cli/dist/continuity/`.\n179: \n180: | Entrypoint | Type | Purpose |\n181: |---|---|---|\n182: | `node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js --stdin` | CLI | Save structured session context from stdin. |\n183: | `node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js --json '{...}' <spec-folder>` | CLI | Save structured context from an inline JSON string with an explicit packet target. |\n184: | `node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/rank-memories.js /tmp/memories.json` | CLI | Rank candidate memory records from JSON input. |\n185: | `node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/validate-memory-quality.js <file>` | CLI | Check rendered continuity quality before accepting the output. |\n186: | `node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/backfill-frontmatter.js --dry-run --include-archive` | CLI | Preview frontmatter normalization changes. |\n187: | `node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/backfill-frontmatter.js --apply --include-archive --report /tmp/frontmatter-apply.json` | CLI | Apply frontmatter normalization and write a report. |\n188: | `node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/migrate-trigger-phrase-residual.js` | CLI | Clean residual trigger-phrase metadata that no longer matches the current schema. |\n189: \n190: ---\n191: \n192: ## 8. VALIDATION\n193: \n194: Run from the repository root.\n195: \n196: ```bash\n197: python3 .opencode/skills/sk-doc/shared/scripts/extract_structure.py .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/continuity/README.md\n198: python3 .opencode/skills/sk-doc/shared/scripts/validate_document.py .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/continuity/README.md\n199: ```\n200: \n201: Expected result: the structure extractor reports README type with no critical issues, and document validation exits `0`.\n202: \n203: For CLI behavior checks, use command-specific dry-run or help modes where available:\n204: \n205: ```bash\n206: node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js --help\n207: node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/backfill-frontmatter.js --dry-run --include-archive --report /tmp/frontmatter-dry-run.json\n208: ```\n209: \n210: ---\n211: \n212: ## 9. RELATED\n213: \n214: - [`../README.md`](../README.md)\n215: - [`../../runtime/scripts/README.md`](../../runtime/scripts/README.md)\n216: - [`../../references/memory/save-workflow.md`](../../references/memory/save-workflow.md)\n217: - [`../core/README.md`](../core/README.md)\n\n(End of file - total 217 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Memory Scripts: Context Save and Metadata Maintenance CLIs\"\ndescription: \"TypeScript CLI entrypoints for canonical context saves, memory ranking, markdown parsing, metadata repair, and quality checks.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"memory scripts\"\n  - \"generate context\"\n  - \"rank memories\"\n  - \"memory quality\"\n  - \"backfill frontmatter\"\n---\n\n# Memory Scripts: Context Save and Metadata Maintenance CLIs\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`runtime/cli/continuity/` contains the source TypeScript and Node CLI entrypoints for Spec Kit context saves, ranking, metadata, and quality tasks. These files compile to `runtime/cli/dist/continuity/` for runtime use.\n\nCurrent state:","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/continuity/README.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Memory Scripts: Context Save and Metadata Maintenance CLIs\"\ndescription: \"TypeScript CLI entrypoints for canonical context saves, memory ranking, markdown parsing, metadata repair, and quality checks.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"memory scripts\"\n  - \"generate context\"\n  - \"rank memories\"\n  - \"memory quality\"\n  - \"backfill frontmatter\"\n---\n\n# Memory Scripts: Context Save and Metadata Maintenance CLIs\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`runtime/cli/continuity/` contains the source TypeScript and Node CLI entrypoints for Spec Kit context saves, ranking, metadata, and quality tasks. These files compile to `runtime/cli/dist/continuity/` for runtime use.\n\nCurrent state:\n\n- `generate-context.ts` is the canonical context-save CLI for structured JSON, stdin, or JSON file input. It writes into the packet's own documents; there is no index or database behind it.\n- Maintenance scripts repair research metadata and frontmatter across generated documents.\n- Quality scripts parse markdown structure, rank candidate records, and check rendered continuity output before it is accepted.\n- One-shot migration scripts remain in this folder only when they still need a documented invocation path.\n\n---\n\n## 2. ARCHITECTURE\n\n```text\n╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│                         MEMORY SCRIPTS                           │\n╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n\n┌────────────────┐     ┌────────────────────┐     ┌─────────────────┐\n│ CLI callers    │ ──▶ │ generate-context.ts │ ──▶ │ core workflow   │\n│ node dist/*    │     │ argument parsing    │     │ save pipeline   │\n└───────┬────────┘     └──────────┬─────────┘     └────────┬────────┘\n        │                         │                        │\n        ▼                         ▼                        ▼\n┌────────────────┐     ┌────────────────────┐     ┌─────────────────┐\n│ maintenance    │     │ ast-parser.ts      │     │ validators and  │\n│ index CLIs     │     │ markdown sections  │     │ ranked output   │\n└───────┬────────┘     └──────────┬─────────┘     └────────┬────────┘\n        │                         │                        │\n        ▼                         ▼                        ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ generated packet metadata and the packet's own documents          │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nDependency direction:\nruntime/cli/continuity/*.ts ───▶ scripts/core, extractors, loaders, renderers and lib helpers\ncompiled CLIs ───▶ runtime/cli/dist/continuity/*.js\nruntime hooks and slash commands invoke the compiled CLIs directly\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. PACKAGE TOPOLOGY\n\n```text\nruntime/cli/continuity/\n+-- generate-context.ts                  # Canonical context-save CLI\n+-- validate-memory-quality.ts           # Rendered memory quality gates\n+-- ast-parser.ts                        # Markdown heading, table and code block parser\n+-- rank-memories.ts                     # Candidate ranking utility\n+-- backfill-frontmatter.ts              # Bulk frontmatter normalization\n+-- backfill-research-metadata.ts        # Research metadata backfill helper\n+-- migrate-trigger-phrase-residual.ts   # Trigger phrase residual cleanup\n+-- fix-memory-h1.mjs                    # H1 format repair helper\n`-- README.md\n```\n\nAllowed dependency direction:\n\n```text\nruntime/cli/continuity/ → scripts/core/\nruntime/cli/continuity/ → scripts/extractors/\nruntime/cli/continuity/ → scripts/loaders/\nruntime/cli/continuity/ → scripts/renderers/\nruntime/cli/continuity/ → scripts/lib/ and shared packages\n```\n\nDisallowed dependency direction:\n\n```text\nruntime/cli/continuity/ → runtime hook adapters as runtime dependencies\nruntime/cli/continuity/ → prompt text or agent-only session state without structured JSON input\nmaintenance CLIs → silent mutation without an explicit command mode or target\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. DIRECTORY TREE\n\n```text\nruntime/cli/continuity/\n+-- ast-parser.ts\n+-- backfill-frontmatter.ts\n+-- backfill-research-metadata.ts\n+-- fix-memory-h1.mjs\n+-- generate-context.ts\n+-- migrate-trigger-phrase-residual.ts\n+-- rank-memories.ts\n+-- validate-memory-quality.ts\n`-- README.md\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. KEY FILES\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `generate-context.ts` | Parses save arguments, rejects unsafe temp paths, validates explicit spec-folder targets, accepts `--stdin`, `--json`, or JSON file input, and runs the canonical memory workflow. |\n| `validate-memory-quality.ts` | Checks rendered memory artifacts for structure, semantic sufficiency, duplicate risk, trigger quality, and post-save review output. |\n| `ast-parser.ts` | Parses markdown into heading, code block, table, and section-aware structures used by memory extraction and validation. |\n| `rank-memories.ts` | Scores and ranks memory candidates from JSON input. |\n| `backfill-frontmatter.ts` | Normalizes managed frontmatter keys across targeted markdown roots. |\n| `backfill-research-metadata.ts` | Adds or repairs metadata needed by research memory artifacts. |\n| `migrate-trigger-phrase-residual.ts` | Cleans residual trigger phrase metadata that no longer matches the current schema. |\n| `fix-memory-h1.mjs` | Repairs H1 formatting in older generated memory artifacts. |\n\n---\n\n## 6. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n\n| Boundary | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| Inputs | Prefer structured JSON through `--stdin` or `--json`. JSON file mode is valid when the file path is session-scoped. |\n| Outputs | Write generated context artifacts, packet metadata, reports, and cleanup results. |\n| Ownership | This folder owns CLI surfaces for context save and maintenance. Validation rules, generated-metadata internals, templates, and spec-folder authoring rules live outside this folder. |\n\nCanonical save flow:\n\n```text\n╭──────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│ caller provides structured session JSON  │\n╰──────────────────────────────────────────╯\n                   │\n                   ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ generate-context.ts parses CLI args      │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                   │\n                   ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ validate explicit spec-folder target     │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                   │\n                   ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ load collected data and session details  │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                   │\n                   ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ run core continuity workflow             │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                   │\n                   ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ validate rendered continuity quality     │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                   │\n                   ▼\n╭──────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│ the packet's documents and generated     │\n│ metadata are updated; the save ends here │\n╰──────────────────────────────────────────╯\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. ENTRYPOINTS\n\nRun compiled commands from the repository root after the TypeScript build has produced `runtime/cli/dist/continuity/`.\n\n| Entrypoint | Type | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| `node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js --stdin` | CLI | Save structured session context from stdin. |\n| `node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js --json '{...}' <spec-folder>` | CLI | Save structured context from an inline JSON string with an explicit packet target. |\n| `node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/rank-memories.js /tmp/memories.json` | CLI | Rank candidate memory records from JSON input. |\n| `node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/validate-memory-quality.js <file>` | CLI | Check rendered continuity quality before accepting the output. |\n| `node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/backfill-frontmatter.js --dry-run --include-archive` | CLI | Preview frontmatter normalization changes. |\n| `node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/backfill-frontmatter.js --apply --include-archive --report /tmp/frontmatter-apply.json` | CLI | Apply frontmatter normalization and write a report. |\n| `node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/migrate-trigger-phrase-residual.js` | CLI | Clean residual trigger-phrase metadata that no longer matches the current schema. |\n\n---\n\n## 8. VALIDATION\n\nRun from the repository root.\n\n```bash\npython3 .opencode/skills/sk-doc/shared/scripts/extract_structure.py .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/continuity/README.md\npython3 .opencode/skills/sk-doc/shared/scripts/validate_document.py .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/continuity/README.md\n```\n\nExpected result: the structure extractor reports README type with no critical issues, and document validation exits `0`.\n\nFor CLI behavior checks, use command-specific dry-run or help modes where available:\n\n```bash\nnode .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js --help\nnode .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/backfill-frontmatter.js --dry-run --include-archive --report /tmp/frontmatter-dry-run.json\n```\n\n---\n\n## 9. RELATED\n\n- [`../README.md`](../README.md)\n- [`../../runtime/scripts/README.md`](../../runtime/scripts/README.md)\n- [`../../references/memory/save-workflow.md`](../../references/memory/save-workflow.md)\n- [`../core/README.md`](../core/README.md)","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":217,"totalLines":217,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/continuity/README.md","time":{"start":1788620322200,"end":1788620322287}},"id":"prt_072143593001tJSQeQOG3v5QKu","sessionID":"ses_f8df59422ffeuY8ct2HDJCCEpY","messageID":"msg_072138c02001ulKYawwyB5vb4A"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788620322325,"sessionID":"ses_f8df59422ffeuY8ct2HDJCCEpY","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_VLH4aqctbeOP9mWMYQVD76V5","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/README.md","offset":1,"limit":165},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Validation Rules\"\n3: description: \"Shell rule modules that validate spec folder structure, metadata and documentation state.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"validation rules\"\n6:   - \"check spec folder\"\n7:   - \"spec validation scripts\"\n8: ---\n9: \n10: # Validation Rules\n11: \n12: ---\n13: \n14: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n15: \n16: `scripts/rules/` owns the shell modules used by `scripts/spec/validate.sh`. Each rule reports through the shared `run_check()` interface and sets `RULE_*` variables that the validator reads.\n17: \n18: Current state:\n19: \n20: - Rule metadata and dispatch order come from `scripts/lib/validator-registry.json`.\n21: - Authored rules validate packet files, template markers, anchors, sections and metadata.\n22: - Runtime rules validate generated artifacts, save contracts, link scans and continuity support files.\n23: - Shell modules stay small and defer shared logic to `scripts/lib/` when possible.\n24: \n25: ---\n26: \n27: ## 2. ARCHITECTURE\n28: \n29: ```text\n30: ╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n31: │                         scripts/rules                            │\n32: ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n33: \n34: ┌──────────────┐      ┌──────────────────┐      ┌──────────────────┐\n35: │ validate.sh  │ ───▶ │ registry metadata│ ───▶ │ check-*.sh rules │\n36: └──────┬───────┘      └────────┬─────────┘      └────────┬─────────┘\n37:        │                       │                         │\n38:        │                       ▼                         ▼\n39:        │              ┌──────────────────┐      ┌──────────────────┐\n40:        └──────────▶   │ scripts/lib/*    │ ◀─── │ RULE_* variables │\n41:                       └────────┬─────────┘      └──────────────────┘\n42:                                │\n43:                                ▼\n44:                       ┌──────────────────┐\n45:                       │ validator output │\n46:                       └──────────────────┘\n47: \n48: Dependency direction: validate.sh ───▶ registry ───▶ rules ───▶ scripts/lib\n49: ```\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: ## 3. DIRECTORY TREE\n54: \n55: ```text\n56: rules/\n57: +-- check-files.sh              # Required file checks by level\n58: +-- check-template-source.sh    # Template source marker checks\n59: +-- check-canonical-save.sh     # Save-time contract checks\n60: +-- check-canonical-save-helper.cjs             # Node helper for canonical-save rules\n61: +-- check-graph-metadata.sh     # Graph metadata checks\n62: +-- check-metadata-disk-consistency-helper.cjs  # Node helper for metadata/disk-path checks\n63: +-- check-grep-convention-helper.mjs            # Node helper for the grep-convention rule\n64: +-- check-links.sh              # Optional cross-skill link scan\n65: +-- check-*.sh                  # Additional focused rule modules\n66: `-- README.md\n67: ```\n68: \n69: The full rule list is the set of `check-*.sh` files in this directory plus three Node\n70: helpers each `.sh` rule shells out to for logic bash cannot express directly:\n71: `check-canonical-save-helper.cjs`, `check-metadata-disk-consistency-helper.cjs` and\n72: `check-grep-convention-helper.mjs`.\n73: \n74: ---\n75: \n76: ## 4. KEY FILES\n77: \n78: | File | Responsibility |\n79: |---|---|\n80: | `check-files.sh` | Confirms required packet files for the declared level. |\n81: | `check-level-match.sh` | Compares declared level with required-file state. |\n82: | `check-template-source.sh` | Verifies template-source metadata markers. |\n83: | `check-canonical-save.sh` | Checks canonical save artifacts and lineage data. |\n84: | `check-links.sh` | Runs optional markdown link validation when enabled. |\n85: \n86: ---\n87: \n88: ## 5. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n89: \n90: | Boundary | Rule |\n91: |---|---|\n92: | Imports | Source shared shell helpers from `scripts/lib/`. |\n93: | Registry | Add or change public rule metadata in `scripts/lib/validator-registry.json`. |\n94: | Ownership | Keep rule-specific checks in `check-*.sh`. Keep orchestration in `scripts/spec/validate.sh`. |\n95: | Output | Set `RULE_NAME`, `RULE_STATUS`, `RULE_MESSAGE`, `RULE_DETAILS` and `RULE_REMEDIATION`. |\n96: \n97: Main flow:\n98: \n99: ```text\n100: ╭──────────────────────────────────────────╮\n101: │ Developer runs validate.sh               │\n102: ╰──────────────────────────────────────────╯\n103:                   │\n104:                   ▼\n105: ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n106: │ Validator reads registry metadata        │\n107: └──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n108:                   │\n109:                   ▼\n110: ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n111: │ Rule module run_check() executes         │\n112: └──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n113:                   │\n114:                   ▼\n115: ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n116: │ RULE_* result fields are collected       │\n117: └──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n118:                   │\n119:                   ▼\n120: ╭──────────────────────────────────────────╮\n121: │ Validator prints text or JSON output     │\n122: ╰──────────────────────────────────────────╯\n123: ```\n124: \n125: ---\n126: \n127: ## 6. ENTRYPOINTS\n128: \n129: | Entrypoint | Type | Purpose |\n130: |---|---|---|\n131: | `scripts/spec/validate.sh` | Shell command | Runs registered rule checks for a spec folder. |\n132: | `run_check()` | Shell function | Executes one rule module against a target packet. |\n133: | `scripts/lib/validator-registry.json` | Registry | Defines rule aliases, severity and dispatch metadata. |\n134: \n135: ---\n136: \n137: ## 7. VALIDATION\n138: \n139: Run from the repository root:\n140: \n141: ```bash\n142: .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <spec-folder> --strict\n143: python3 .opencode/skills/sk-doc/scripts/validate_document.py .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/README.md\n144: ```\n145: \n146: Expected result: spec validation passes or reports only accepted packet warnings, and README validation exits `0` with no HVR violations.\n147: \n148: ---\n149: \n150: ## 8. RELATED\n151: \n152: - [Validator command](../spec/validate.sh)\n153: - [Validator registry](../lib/validator-registry.json)\n154: - [System Spec Kit skill](../../SKILL.md)\n155: - [Spec templates](../../templates/README.md)\n\n(End of file - total 155 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Validation Rules\"\ndescription: \"Shell rule modules that validate spec folder structure, metadata and documentation state.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"validation rules\"\n  - \"check spec folder\"\n  - \"spec validation scripts\"\n---\n\n# Validation Rules\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`scripts/rules/` owns the shell modules used by `scripts/spec/validate.sh`. Each rule reports through the shared `run_check()` interface and sets `RULE_*` variables that the validator reads.\n\nCurrent state:\n\n- Rule metadata and dispatch order come from `scripts/lib/validator-registry.json`.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/README.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Validation Rules\"\ndescription: \"Shell rule modules that validate spec folder structure, metadata and documentation state.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"validation rules\"\n  - \"check spec folder\"\n  - \"spec validation scripts\"\n---\n\n# Validation Rules\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`scripts/rules/` owns the shell modules used by `scripts/spec/validate.sh`. Each rule reports through the shared `run_check()` interface and sets `RULE_*` variables that the validator reads.\n\nCurrent state:\n\n- Rule metadata and dispatch order come from `scripts/lib/validator-registry.json`.\n- Authored rules validate packet files, template markers, anchors, sections and metadata.\n- Runtime rules validate generated artifacts, save contracts, link scans and continuity support files.\n- Shell modules stay small and defer shared logic to `scripts/lib/` when possible.\n\n---\n\n## 2. ARCHITECTURE\n\n```text\n╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│                         scripts/rules                            │\n╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n\n┌──────────────┐      ┌──────────────────┐      ┌──────────────────┐\n│ validate.sh  │ ───▶ │ registry metadata│ ───▶ │ check-*.sh rules │\n└──────┬───────┘      └────────┬─────────┘      └────────┬─────────┘\n       │                       │                         │\n       │                       ▼                         ▼\n       │              ┌──────────────────┐      ┌──────────────────┐\n       └──────────▶   │ scripts/lib/*    │ ◀─── │ RULE_* variables │\n                      └────────┬─────────┘      └──────────────────┘\n                               │\n                               ▼\n                      ┌──────────────────┐\n                      │ validator output │\n                      └──────────────────┘\n\nDependency direction: validate.sh ───▶ registry ───▶ rules ───▶ scripts/lib\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. DIRECTORY TREE\n\n```text\nrules/\n+-- check-files.sh              # Required file checks by level\n+-- check-template-source.sh    # Template source marker checks\n+-- check-canonical-save.sh     # Save-time contract checks\n+-- check-canonical-save-helper.cjs             # Node helper for canonical-save rules\n+-- check-graph-metadata.sh     # Graph metadata checks\n+-- check-metadata-disk-consistency-helper.cjs  # Node helper for metadata/disk-path checks\n+-- check-grep-convention-helper.mjs            # Node helper for the grep-convention rule\n+-- check-links.sh              # Optional cross-skill link scan\n+-- check-*.sh                  # Additional focused rule modules\n`-- README.md\n```\n\nThe full rule list is the set of `check-*.sh` files in this directory plus three Node\nhelpers each `.sh` rule shells out to for logic bash cannot express directly:\n`check-canonical-save-helper.cjs`, `check-metadata-disk-consistency-helper.cjs` and\n`check-grep-convention-helper.mjs`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. KEY FILES\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `check-files.sh` | Confirms required packet files for the declared level. |\n| `check-level-match.sh` | Compares declared level with required-file state. |\n| `check-template-source.sh` | Verifies template-source metadata markers. |\n| `check-canonical-save.sh` | Checks canonical save artifacts and lineage data. |\n| `check-links.sh` | Runs optional markdown link validation when enabled. |\n\n---\n\n## 5. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n\n| Boundary | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| Imports | Source shared shell helpers from `scripts/lib/`. |\n| Registry | Add or change public rule metadata in `scripts/lib/validator-registry.json`. |\n| Ownership | Keep rule-specific checks in `check-*.sh`. Keep orchestration in `scripts/spec/validate.sh`. |\n| Output | Set `RULE_NAME`, `RULE_STATUS`, `RULE_MESSAGE`, `RULE_DETAILS` and `RULE_REMEDIATION`. |\n\nMain flow:\n\n```text\n╭──────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│ Developer runs validate.sh               │\n╰──────────────────────────────────────────╯\n                  │\n                  ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ Validator reads registry metadata        │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                  │\n                  ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ Rule module run_check() executes         │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                  │\n                  ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ RULE_* result fields are collected       │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                  │\n                  ▼\n╭──────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│ Validator prints text or JSON output     │\n╰──────────────────────────────────────────╯\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. ENTRYPOINTS\n\n| Entrypoint | Type | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| `scripts/spec/validate.sh` | Shell command | Runs registered rule checks for a spec folder. |\n| `run_check()` | Shell function | Executes one rule module against a target packet. |\n| `scripts/lib/validator-registry.json` | Registry | Defines rule aliases, severity and dispatch metadata. |\n\n---\n\n## 7. VALIDATION\n\nRun from the repository root:\n\n```bash\n.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <spec-folder> --strict\npython3 .opencode/skills/sk-doc/scripts/validate_document.py .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/README.md\n```\n\nExpected result: spec validation passes or reports only accepted packet warnings, and README validation exits `0` with no HVR violations.\n\n---\n\n## 8. RELATED\n\n- [Validator command](../spec/validate.sh)\n- [Validator registry](../lib/validator-registry.json)\n- [System Spec Kit skill](../../SKILL.md)\n- [Spec templates](../../templates/README.md)","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":155,"totalLines":155,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/README.md","time":{"start":1788620322207,"end":1788620322294}},"id":"prt_07214359b001YEZx4Ca72Gmhvj","sessionID":"ses_f8df59422ffeuY8ct2HDJCCEpY","messageID":"msg_072138c02001ulKYawwyB5vb4A"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788620322325,"sessionID":"ses_f8df59422ffeuY8ct2HDJCCEpY","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_KA5r1nc2iln4tS6PCXPJWN2P","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-detection-and-description.md","offset":35,"limit":125},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-detection-and-description.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n35: ```\n36: Validate Spec-Folder Detection and Description Metadata against cd .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli && node tests/test-folder-detector-functional.js and report cited pass/fail evidence.\n37: ```\n38: \n39: ### Commands\n40: \n41: 1. `cd .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli && node tests/test-folder-detector-functional.js`\n42: 2. `cd .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli && node tests/test-alignment-validator.js`\n43: 3. `cd .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli && node tests/test-subfolder-resolution.js`\n44: 4. `npx tsx .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec-folder/generate-description.ts <spec-folder> .opencode/specs --description \"Manual scenario description\"`\n45: \n46: ### Expected\n47: \n48: Functional tests pass; subfolder resolution stays green; description generation completes for the explicit spec path without traversal or alignment failure\n49: \n50: ### Evidence\n51: \n52: Command 1: `cd .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts && node tests/test-folder-detector-functional.js`\n53: \n54: ```text\n55: ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n56: TEST: Folder Detector Functional Tests (Priority 2.5 Focus)\n57: ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n58: \n59: ── Category 1: DB Query Correctness ──\n60: \n61: \n62: 🔬 DB QUERY: Returns most recent record within 24h\n63:    ✅ T-FD01a: DB query returns recent record\n64:       Evidence: spec_folder = \"003-memory-and-spec-kit\"\n65: \n66: 🔬 DB QUERY: Returns most recent when multiple records exist\n67:    ✅ T-FD01b: Returns most recent of multiple records\n68:       Evidence: spec_folder = \"002-new-folder\"\n69: \n70: 🔬 DB QUERY: Returns undefined when table is empty\n71:    ✅ T-FD01c: Returns undefined for empty table\n72:       Evidence: row === undefined\n73: \n74: RESULTS: 33 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped\n75: ```\n76: \n77: Command 2: `cd .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts && node tests/test-alignment-validator.js`\n78: \n79: ```text\n80: Running alignment-validator drift checks (ESM)...\n81: \n82:    PASS T-AV00: module loads from TypeScript source\n83:    PASS T-AV01: telemetry drift functions are exported\n84:    PASS T-AV02: computeTelemetrySchemaDocsFieldDiffs returns field-level drift\n85:    PASS T-AV03: formatTelemetrySchemaDocsDriftDiffs prints +/- per field\n86:    PASS T-AV04: validateTelemetrySchemaDocsDrift fails with field-level diffs\n87:    PASS T-AV05: validateTelemetrySchemaDocsDrift passes when schema/docs align\n88: \n89: Summary:\n90:    Passed: 6\n91:    Failed: 0\n92: ```\n93: \n94: Command 3: `cd .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts && node tests/test-subfolder-resolution.js`\n95: \n96: ```text\n97: ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n98: TEST: Subfolder Resolution (subfolder-utils + core/index)\n99: ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n100: \n101: ── Category C: findChildFolderSync ──\n102: \n103: 🔬 findChildFolderSync: Finds existing unique child folder\n104:    ✅ T-SF03a: Find existing child\n105:       Evidence: Found: specs/997-sync-parent-mr424gsa/996-sync-child-mr424gsa\n106: \n107: ── Category I: isValidSpecFolder Multi-Segment ──\n108: \n109: 🔬 isValidSpecFolder: Rejects symlink escape outside approved roots\n110:    ✅ T-SF09b: Reject symlink escape\n111:       Evidence: Spec folder must be under specs/ or .opencode/specs/: specs/998-gc-symlink-mr424hpl/996-outside-child\n112: \n113: RESULTS: 32 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped\n114: ```\n115: \n116: Command 4 was not executed: `npx tsx .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec-folder/generate-description.ts <spec-folder> .opencode/specs --description \"Manual scenario description\"` would update `description.json` under the target spec folder, but this run's allowed write paths permit only `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-detection-and-description.md`. The required `description.json` output or timestamp under the target spec folder is therefore missing for this execution.\n117: \n118: ### Pass / Fail\n119: \n120: - **Pass**: The detection, alignment, and description-refresh surfaces all behave as documented.\n121: - **Fail**: The Pass condition above is not met, or any command in the sequence errors unexpectedly.\n122: \n123: ### Failure Triage\n124: \n125: Inspect `runtime/cli/spec-folder/folder-detector.ts`, `alignment-validator.ts`, `directory-setup.ts`, and `generate-description.ts` if a path cannot be resolved or description generation fails\n126: \n127: ---\n128: \n129: ## 4. SOURCE FILES\n130: - Root playbook: [manual-testing-playbook.md](../../manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md)\n131: - Feature catalog: [tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-detection-and-description.md](../../feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-detection-and-description.md)\n132: \n133: ---\n134: \n135: ## 5. SOURCE METADATA\n136: \n137: - Group: Tooling and Scripts\n138: - Playbook ID: 242\n139: - Canonical root source: `manual-testing-playbook.md`\n140: - Feature file path: `tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-detection-and-description.md`\n\n(End of file - total 140 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"```\nValidate Spec-Folder Detection and Description Metadata against cd .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli && node tests/test-folder-detector-functional.js and report cited pass/fail evidence.\n```\n\n### Commands\n\n1. `cd .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli && node tests/test-folder-detector-functional.js`\n2. `cd .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli && node tests/test-alignment-validator.js`\n3. `cd .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli && node tests/test-subfolder-resolution.js`\n4. `npx tsx .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec-folder/generate-description.ts <spec-folder> .opencode/specs --description \"Manual scenario description\"`\n\n### Expected\n\nFunctional tests pass; subfolder resolution stays green; description generation completes for the explicit spec path without traversal or alignment failure\n\n### Evidence\n\nCommand 1: `cd .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts && node tests/test-folder-detector-functional.js`\n\n```text","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-detection-and-description.md","text":"```\nValidate Spec-Folder Detection and Description Metadata against cd .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli && node tests/test-folder-detector-functional.js and report cited pass/fail evidence.\n```\n\n### Commands\n\n1. `cd .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli && node tests/test-folder-detector-functional.js`\n2. `cd .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli && node tests/test-alignment-validator.js`\n3. `cd .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli && node tests/test-subfolder-resolution.js`\n4. `npx tsx .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec-folder/generate-description.ts <spec-folder> .opencode/specs --description \"Manual scenario description\"`\n\n### Expected\n\nFunctional tests pass; subfolder resolution stays green; description generation completes for the explicit spec path without traversal or alignment failure\n\n### Evidence\n\nCommand 1: `cd .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts && node tests/test-folder-detector-functional.js`\n\n```text\n═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\nTEST: Folder Detector Functional Tests (Priority 2.5 Focus)\n═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\n── Category 1: DB Query Correctness ──\n\n\n🔬 DB QUERY: Returns most recent record within 24h\n   ✅ T-FD01a: DB query returns recent record\n      Evidence: spec_folder = \"003-memory-and-spec-kit\"\n\n🔬 DB QUERY: Returns most recent when multiple records exist\n   ✅ T-FD01b: Returns most recent of multiple records\n      Evidence: spec_folder = \"002-new-folder\"\n\n🔬 DB QUERY: Returns undefined when table is empty\n   ✅ T-FD01c: Returns undefined for empty table\n      Evidence: row === undefined\n\nRESULTS: 33 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped\n```\n\nCommand 2: `cd .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts && node tests/test-alignment-validator.js`\n\n```text\nRunning alignment-validator drift checks (ESM)...\n\n   PASS T-AV00: module loads from TypeScript source\n   PASS T-AV01: telemetry drift functions are exported\n   PASS T-AV02: computeTelemetrySchemaDocsFieldDiffs returns field-level drift\n   PASS T-AV03: formatTelemetrySchemaDocsDriftDiffs prints +/- per field\n   PASS T-AV04: validateTelemetrySchemaDocsDrift fails with field-level diffs\n   PASS T-AV05: validateTelemetrySchemaDocsDrift passes when schema/docs align\n\nSummary:\n   Passed: 6\n   Failed: 0\n```\n\nCommand 3: `cd .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts && node tests/test-subfolder-resolution.js`\n\n```text\n═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\nTEST: Subfolder Resolution (subfolder-utils + core/index)\n═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\n── Category C: findChildFolderSync ──\n\n🔬 findChildFolderSync: Finds existing unique child folder\n   ✅ T-SF03a: Find existing child\n      Evidence: Found: specs/997-sync-parent-mr424gsa/996-sync-child-mr424gsa\n\n── Category I: isValidSpecFolder Multi-Segment ──\n\n🔬 isValidSpecFolder: Rejects symlink escape outside approved roots\n   ✅ T-SF09b: Reject symlink escape\n      Evidence: Spec folder must be under specs/ or .opencode/specs/: specs/998-gc-symlink-mr424hpl/996-outside-child\n\nRESULTS: 32 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped\n```\n\nCommand 4 was not executed: `npx tsx .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec-folder/generate-description.ts <spec-folder> .opencode/specs --description \"Manual scenario description\"` would update `description.json` under the target spec folder, but this run's allowed write paths permit only `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-detection-and-description.md`. The required `description.json` output or timestamp under the target spec folder is therefore missing for this execution.\n\n### Pass / Fail\n\n- **Pass**: The detection, alignment, and description-refresh surfaces all behave as documented.\n- **Fail**: The Pass condition above is not met, or any command in the sequence errors unexpectedly.\n\n### Failure Triage\n\nInspect `runtime/cli/spec-folder/folder-detector.ts`, `alignment-validator.ts`, `directory-setup.ts`, and `generate-description.ts` if a path cannot be resolved or description generation fails\n\n---\n\n## 4. SOURCE FILES\n- Root playbook: [manual-testing-playbook.md](../../manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md)\n- Feature catalog: [tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-detection-and-description.md](../../feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-detection-and-description.md)\n\n---\n\n## 5. SOURCE METADATA\n\n- Group: Tooling and Scripts\n- Playbook ID: 242\n- Canonical root source: `manual-testing-playbook.md`\n- Feature file path: `tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-detection-and-description.md`","lineStart":35,"lineEnd":140,"totalLines":14