{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788620511540,"sessionID":"ses_f8df59422ffeuY8ct2HDJCCEpY","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_xl0VZ1o9OdDrBJ5aUQf2AiUJ","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/specs/system-speckit/054-decommission-debt-fixes/002-scripts-into-runtime-nesting/review/lineages/luna-max-review-2/iterations/iteration-001.md\n+# Iteration 1: Correctness and Package Topology\n+\n+## Focus\n+Correctness review of the nested workspace, package scripts, lockfile, test discovery and primary moved entrypoints. Current source state was read directly. No target files were modified.\n+\n+## Scorecard\n+- Dimensions covered: correctness\n+- Files reviewed: 12 direct files plus the 453-entry manifest\n+- New findings: P0=0 P1=1 P2=1\n+- Refined findings: P0=0 P1=0 P2=0\n+- New findings ratio: 0.40\n+\n+## Findings\n+\n+### P1, Required\n+- **F001**: The root workspace's `test:root` delegates to `npm run test --workspace=@spec-kit/cli`, but the CLI package's `test` command invokes `vitest run --config ../vitest.config.ts --root .`, while the root `vitest.config.ts` is a multi-project config rooted at the skill package and has a separate CLI project. This split means the package-local command does not use the root multi-project configuration and is not proven by the packet's root test claim to execute the same test surface. The repository has a dedicated `runtime/cli/vitest.config.ts` absent from the package scripts. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/package.json:19-24] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/package.json:18-21] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/vitest.config.ts:19-57] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/vitest.config.ts:13-39]\n+\n+### P2, Suggestion\n+- **F002**: The package boundary is now structurally coherent, but the moved package's source-facing documentation still describes the old package topology, which makes future path repairs error-prone. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/README.md:56-98]\n+\n+## Cross-Reference Results\n+| Protocol | Status | Gate | Evidence | Notes |\n+|----------|--------|------|----------|-------|\n+| spec_code | partial | hard | spec.md:42-50; package.json:6-25 | Target layout is implemented, but test command contract needs one authoritative config path. |\n+| checklist_evidence | partial | hard | tasks.md:111-125; implementation-summary.md:208-231 | Completion claims list broad test gates without an inline proof for the package-local config split. |\n+| feature_catalog_code | partial | advisory | runtime/cli/README.md:56-98 | Current entrypoints exist, while topology text is stale. |\n+| playbook_capability | partial | advisory | runtime/cli/package.json:18-21 | Test commands are executable-looking but their config ownership is ambiguous. |\n+\n+## Assessment\n+- New findings ratio: 0.40\n+- Dimensions addressed: correctness\n+- Novelty justification: package and lockfile existence was confirmed in the current tree, so the earlier missing-manifest finding is not carried forward; the remaining issue is a current test-config contract mismatch.\n+\n+## Ruled Out\n+- Missing `runtime/cli/package.json` was ruled out by direct path inspection and the current workspace manifest. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/package.json:6-10] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/package.json:1-34]\n+\n+## Dead Ends\n+- Repository test execution was not attempted because this detached lineage may write outside the lineage directory.\n+\n+## Recommended Next Focus\n+Security and path-boundary review of root discovery, hook candidate resolution, fixed-depth path calculations and symlink/containment handling.\n+\n+Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\n*** Add File: /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/specs/system-speckit/054-decommission-debt-fixes/002-scripts-into-runtime-nesting/review/lineages/luna-max-review-2/deltas/iter-001.jsonl\n+{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"run\":1,\"iteration\":1,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"correctness-package-topology\",\"dimensions\":[\"correctness\"],\"filesReviewed\":[\".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/package.json\",\".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/package.json\",\".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/vitest.config.ts\",\".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/vitest.config.ts\",\".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/README.md\",\".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/package-lock.json\"],\"findingsCount\":2,\"findingsSummary\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":1,\"P2\":1},\"findingsNew\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":1,\"P2\":1},\"findingDetails\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"category\":\"correctness\",\"dimension\":\"correctness\",\"title\":\"CLI package test command and root multi-project test configuration are not one proven contract\",\"file\":\".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/package.json\",\"line\":18,\"evidence\":\"The CLI package invokes ../vitest.config.ts while the root config defines a separate runtime/cli-rooted project and the runtime config excludes runtime/cli.\",\"recommendation\":\"Choose one authoritative CLI Vitest config and make the package and root gates invoke it explicitly.\",\"disposition\":\"active\",\"findingClass\":\"test-isolation\",\"scopeProof\":\"Read the root package manifest, CLI manifest, root Vitest config and runtime Vitest config.\",\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"workspace test gate\",\"CLI package test script\"],\"content_hash\":\"f001-correctness-cli-vitest-contract\"},{\"id\":\"F002\",\"severity\":\"P2\",\"category\":\"maintainability\",\"dimension\":\"correctness\",\"title\":\"Moved package README retains stale scripts topology\",\"file\":\".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/README.md\",\"line\":59,\"evidence\":\"The package is at runtime/cli, but the topology block begins with scripts/ and lists memory/.\",\"recommendation\":\"Rewrite the package topology block to use runtime/cli and continuity.\",\"disposition\":\"active\",\"findingClass\":\"cross-consumer\",\"scopeProof\":\"Read the moved package README and package manifest.\",\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"operator documentation\",\"future path maintenance\"],\"content_hash\":\"f002-maintainability-cli-readme-topology\"}],\"newFindingsRatio\":0.4,\"traceabilityChecks\":{\"summary\":{\"required\":2,\"executed\":2,\"pass\":0,\"partial\":2,\"fail\":0,\"blocked\":0,\"notApplicable\":0,\"gatingFailures\":0},\"results\":[{\"protocolId\":\"spec_code\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"gateClass\":\"hard\",\"applicable\":true,\"counts\":{\"pass\":0,\"partial\":1,\"fail\":0,\"skipped\":0},\"evidence\":[\"spec.md:42-50\",\"package.json:6-25\"],\"findingRefs\":[\"F001\"],\"summary\":\"Layout is present but test-config ownership is ambiguous.\"},{\"protocolId\":\"checklist_evidence\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"gateClass\":\"hard\",\"applicable\":true,\"counts\":{\"pass\":0,\"partial\":1,\"fail\":0,\"skipped\":0},\"evidence\":[\"tasks.md:111-125\",\"implementation-summary.md:208-231\"],\"findingRefs\":[\"F001\"],\"summary\":\"Broad test claims lack config-specific proof.\"},{\"protocolId\":\"feature_catalog_code\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"gateClass\":\"advisory\",\"applicable\":true,\"counts\":{\"pass\":0,\"partial\":1,\"fail\":0,\"skipped\":0},\"evidence\":[\"runtime/cli/README.md:56-98\"],\"findingRefs\":[\"F002\"],\"summary\":\"Current entrypoints exist but topology text is stale.\"},{\"protocolId\":\"playbook_capability\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"gateClass\":\"advisory\",\"applicable\":true,\"counts\":{\"pass\":0,\"partial\":1,\"fail\":0,\"skipped\":0},\"evidence\":[\"runtime/cli/package.json:18-21\"],\"findingRefs\":[\"F001\"],\"summary\":\"CLI test invocation is not tied to one explicitly named config.\"}]},\"reviewDepthSchemaVersion\":2,\"reviewDepthApplicability\":{\"scopeClass\":\"complex\",\"enforcement\":\"stri